    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Marketing-Assistant--Student-_R5003": {
      "title": "Marketing Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: Open exclusively to AU students, the Marketing and Publications Assistant works closely with the American University Museum’s Marketing and Publications Specialist to support social media, marketing, and communications for the museum’s seasonal exhibitions and programs. The primary focus of this position is social media marketing. The assistant will gather information and materials from artists, curators, and museum staff; identify the most compelling aspects of exhibitions and programs; and translate that information into engaging, accessible promotional content for museum audiences. Responsibilities include developing a strategic social media schedule, writing promotional copy, creating and sourcing visual content, photographing exhibitions and events, and scheduling posts in advance through Hootsuite. The position may also assist with email marketing and developing promotional content for email campaigns. This role is well suited to a creative, responsible, and self-directed student who can work effectively in an environment where priorities and assignments may evolve. The ideal candidate is comfortable taking initiative, making thoughtful decisions about content, and keeping the Marketing and Publications Specialist informed about the status of ongoing projects, questions, and deadlines. Essential Functions: Gather information and materials from artists, curators, and museum staff. Identify the most compelling aspects of exhibitions and programs and translate that information into engaging, accessible promotional content for museum audiences. Develop a strategic social media schedule. Write promotional copy. Create and source visual content. Photograph exhibitions and events. Schedule posts in advance through Hootsuite. Assist with email marketing and developing promotional content for email campaigns. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 - 15 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $23.50 per hour. Preferred Education and Experience: Marketing, public relations, communications, art, and art history students are especially encouraged to apply. Excellent writing skills, with an ability to identify the most important and compelling information in longer written materials and transform it into concise, engaging promotional copy. Knowledge of social media marketing and an understanding of how content and messaging can be adapted for different audiences. Strong visual judgment and a good design aesthetic; proficiency in Canva required. Experience with Adobe Creative Suite is desirable. Highly responsible, organized, and attentive to deadlines. Able to work independently and effectively in a flexible, sometimes unstructured environment. Strong communication skills, including a willingness to provide regular status updates, ask questions when needed, and flag potential problems before deadlines are affected. Comfortable communicating professionally with artists, curators, museum staff, and other collaborators. Photography and social media video experience is a plus. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Hybrid position, approximately 15 hours per week, with a combination of on-site work at the museum and remote work. Occasional weekend hours may be requested to photograph, film, or attend museum events. Museum marketing is deadline-driven and often involves managing several projects at once. The successful candidate must be dependable, organized, and proactive about communicating progress, questions, potential problems, and anticipated delays. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/ATEC-Studio-Assistant--Student---FWS-_R4983": {
      "title": "ATEC Studio Assistant (Student) (FWS)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Audio Technology Program seeks a part-time undergraduate work-study ATEC Studio Assistant to support day-to-day operations in the ATEC Recording Studio. The candidate must have completed or be currently enrolled in ATEC 415/615, Sound Studio Techniques. In addition, we seek an individual who demonstrates strong organizational skills, is punctual, detail oriented, and has the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic and creative environment. Essential Functions: Support day-to-day operations in the ATEC Recording Studio. Other duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 6 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Current AU student with an active Federal Work Study (FWS) award. The candidate must have completed or be currently enrolled in ATEC 415/615, Sound Studio Techniques. Demonstrate strong organizational skills, is punctual, detail oriented, and has the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic and creative environment. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Interim-Medical-Director_R5002": {
      "title": "Interim Medical Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Student Affairs and Dean of Students Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Full On Campus Presence Union: Job Description: Summary: The Interim Medical Director oversees the delivery of healthcare services to undergraduate, graduate, and law students of American University handling approximately 12,000 visits per year. The Interim Medical Director of the Student Health Center leads the strategic planning, implementation, and delivery of healthcare services to American University students. The Interim Medical Director develops policies and procedures in accordance with District of Columbia and federal regulations to assure a safe and effective campus health program; works collaboratively with campus partners and local public health authorities to manage campus health epidemics and to enhance departmental operations that support student health needs; develops and monitors budgets; oversees the Student Health Insurance Plan; serves as a resource for the campus community on issues of health promotion, disease prevention, safety, and health advocacy; monitors and assesses the effectiveness of programs and services; and manages staff. The Interim Medical Director ensures that the Center follows the guidelines and standards established by the AAAHC accreditation body to maintain its accreditation, and benchmarks with college health colleagues to ensure best practice service delivery.  The Interim Medical Director acts as a clinical expert and role model for clinical staff and clinical supervision over the advanced practice clinicians. The Interim Medical Director oversees eight clinical staff and four administrative staff and manages an annual budget of $1.2 million including $350,000 in revenue targets. The Interim Medical Director also oversees a $5 million Student Health Insurance Plan. Essential Functions: 1.) Administrative and Clinical Leadership Develop, implement, and evaluate Center’s policies and procedures. Oversee the Associate Director of Administrative Services’ negotiation, administration, and management of the Student Health Insurance Program in consultation with Risk Management, Procurement, and the Division of Student Affairs. Provide preventive healthcare programs to the campus community and make appropriate referrals to off-campus resources. Facilitate workshops for new student orientation, resident assistants, student leaders, faculty, and staff. Develop budgets for Center that provide adequate breadth and depth of clinical care and outreach consultation and training; assure compliance with ACHA standards of care and AAAHC accreditation requirements. Interpret, implement, and monitor compliance with District of Columbia and federal laws related to healthcare delivery including medical staff credentialing, immunization requirements, reporting of epidemics/contagious diseases, and other public health matters; represent the university to the DC Department of Health, Centers for Disease Control and other external agencies. Alongside the Associate Medical Director, fully investigate all adverse incidents and take corrective action, as appropriate. Oversee clinical care including primary and psychiatric care, quality improvement, outreach and consultation, chart review, and risk management. Work closely with Risk Management to ensure full compliance with safety protocols, insurance mandates, hazardous waste disposal, and malpractice concerns. Promote and develop best clinical practices to meet the mission and vision of the Center and university whereby staff understand, comply, and support the vision through the development, interpretation, and execution of policies and procedures. Maintain the Center’s healthcare accreditation. Provide leadership in departmental strategic planning activities, program review activities, and assessment of learning outcomes. Identify quality improvement opportunities, service improvements, and emerging trends for clinical service delivery. Oversee medication dispensary and lab operations. Oversee the selection and administration of the student health insurance plan. 2.) Direct Patient Care Provides primary health care services within scope of practice available through the Student Health Center ensuring that care is appropriate to the age, culture, and individual needs of the patient. Obtains health histories and performs physical exams. Diagnoses and manages acute and chronic health conditions in partnership with the patient. Orders, conducts, and interprets diagnostic studies and lab tests. Performs diagnostic and therapeutic procedures including suturing, wound care, incision and drainage, splinting, casting, biopsies, and cryotherapy. Prescribes and recommends pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies, including controlled medications, in accordance with applicable laws. Follows standard charting procedures as determined by clinic policy and participates in chart and peer review. Assures adequate follow-up. Teaches and counsels patients, as indicated. Promotes self-care through the provision of information, counseling, and education. Teaches health promotion, wellness, and disease prevention. 3.) Staff Management/Professional Development Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate direct reports. Actively engage in professional development activities and encourage professional development of Center staff. Contribute to the overall efforts of the Division of Student Affairs by establishing and maintaining partnerships with all areas of the division and by participating in project teams, events, and activities of the division. Encourage Center staff to participate in campus activities. 4.) Consultation/Advocacy Coordinate campus medical response in health and safety emergencies. Serve as a resource and consultant to the campus community on issues related to student health and healthcare delivery. Serves on the university’s Communicable Infectious Disease Response Team.  Coordinate with campus partners including the Office of the Dean of Students, Center for Well-Being and Psychological Services, Housing and Residence Life, Academic Support and Access Center, Risk Management, Enrollment Management, New Student and Family Programs, Public Safety, Student Accounts, and other departments to address students’ comprehensive health and wellness needs. Serve on Division of Student Affairs and University committees including, but not limited to, the Care Team and Emergency Preparedness Committee. Serve as liaison to Student Government; respond to requests from student media in collaboration with University Communications and Marketing. 5.) Other Duties as Assigned Serve on Divisional Committees and provide leadership presence at university events such as Orientation, Commencement, Convocation and Family Weekend as requested. Supervisory Responsibility: This position reports directly to the Assistant Vice President of Student Affairs and Dean of Students. Reporting directly to the Interim Medical Director is the Associate Director for Administrative Services, the Associate Medical Director, the Administrative Coordinator, and the University Psychiatrist. The Interim Medical Director supervises the Associate Director for Administrative Services and the Associate Medical Director, who oversees compliance with District of Columbia and federal laws related to medical staff credentialing, immunization requirements, reporting of epidemics/contagious diseases, and other public health matters, and represents the university to the DC Department of Health. The Interim Medical Director indirectly supervises the Administrative Coordinator’s configuration and management of the electronic medical record system and ensures that appropriate provisions for confidentiality and HIPAA compliance are in place.  Competencies: Building and Supporting Teams. Championing Customer Needs. Developing Plans. Evaluating and Implementing Ideas. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Managing Talent. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time 35 hours per week. Full presence interim position with occasional evening and weekend hours. Salary Range: $200,000.00 - $225,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: M.D. or D.O. 8 - 10 years of relevant experience. Preferred Education and Experience: 10+ years of relevant experience. Travel Required: Occasional travel for professional development may be required. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Licensed physician (M.D. or D.O.) or license-eligible in the District of Columbia with unrestricted license to practice. Board-certified in internal medicine, family practice, adolescent medicine, or pediatrics. Possess and maintain a valid Drug Enforcement Agency (DEA) certificate and number to prescribe medication and controlled substances. Substantive professional experience in clinical management, quality improvement, and supervision. Demonstrated expertise developing and implementing evidence-based programs to support healthcare delivery.  Significant experience with FERPA and HIPAA compliance as well as advocacy for student healthcare needs. Proven ability to respond effectively to healthcare emergencies/epidemics and to work collaboratively with campus and community responders. Must have knowledge of primary and psychiatric care systems including best practice standards of care. Evidence of an effective leadership style and background demonstrating success in working with clinical staff, students, parents, administrators, faculty, and alumni. Ability to think strategically and proactively. Proven ability to work across organizational boundaries as an effective member of a team. Significant experience managing staff and budgets and experience supervising professional staff. Evidence of ability to plan and implement programs. Excellent interpersonal skills; ability to manage multiple, competing priorities; demonstrated computer proficiency including personal productivity software and electronic medical record systems; strong analytical skills; and excellent communication skills are required. Current knowledge of principles/practices of healthcare delivery including regulatory requirements and accreditation standards. Student service orientation with experience working with diverse populations including international students, LGBTQIA+ students, students with disabilities, veterans, and non-traditional students. Demonstrated skill in managing difficult situations involving students, parents, staff, faculty, and community agencies. Must have highest standards of integrity and ethics in both performance and behavior. Desire and appreciation for work in a diverse, fast-paced office environment. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/SOC-Tech-Support--Student-_R4991": {
      "title": "SOC Tech Support (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: School of Communication Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: SOC Technology Services is seeking motivated undergraduate and graduate student employees to join our team for Spring 2026. Student Support Assistants will be cross-trained to work across various help desks and technology spaces within the School of Communication (SOC). This is a hands-on position ideal for students interested in gaining experience in customer support, media equipment, and classroom technology. Essential Functions: 1.) SubHub Technology Support Desk (McKinley Building) Provide on-call assistance for faculty and staff regarding classroom technology issues. Answer our help desk phone and troubleshoot classroom tech-related questions or errors. 2.) Doyle/Forman Theater Support (Mckinley Building) Operate basic projection system and AV equipment during classes and in the theater. Provide assistance to faculty using the space, ensure the food/drink policies are met and perform opening/closing procedures of the space. 3.) Cage Equipment Desk (Media Production Center) Staff the equipment checkout desk and assist with equipment check-ins/returns. Perform basic equipment inspections and help transfer gear (as able). 4.) Live Event Support (Mckinley Building) Assist with setup and basic operation of studio equipment. Provide in-room support for ongoing classes and events. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 15 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $19.00 per hour. Preferred Education and Experience: Familiarity with classroom A/V systems, media production gear, or customer service. Communication and problem-solving skills. Willingness to learn and provide support across different environments. ​​ Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Flexible scheduling available based on student availability and course schedule. Opportunities for continued employment during the academic year. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
