    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Ivy-City-Research-Assistant--Student-_R5106": {
      "title": "Ivy City Research Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: This research assistant will work with Professor Meltzer on data collection, analysis, and community report-back on a community-based environmental just research project in Ivy City in partnership with Empower DC. The RA will assist with note-taking during in-depth interviews with residents, conduct coding and thematic analysis, help draft a peer-reviewed manuscript, prepare a poster and/or slides for academic conference presentations, and prepare materials for a community report-back of study findings. This position runs from Sept 25, 2026 - December 15, 2026. The RA will assist with note-taking, transcribing transcripts, and thematic analysis of in-depth interviews with residents of Ivy City on their environmental exposures. The RA will then assist with the write-up of a scientific manuscript and the preparation of posters and/or slides for academic conference presentations, as well as preparing for community report-back events with Empower DC.  Essential Functions: Interview note taking. Transcription. Thematic analysis. Manuscript preparation. Conference presentation preparation. Community report-back event. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 20 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.95 per hour. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Current--Student-_R5102": {
      "title": "Current (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: School of Communication Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: Current   seeks an advanced undergraduate or graduate student in journalism to research and report on issues affecting public media in the United States. Successful candidates will have strong writing skills; an interest in thinking analytically about media and how it is funded, created and distributed; and the ability to collaborate on various aspects of news reporting and publishing.  Current   is an independent news service covering public media, including NPR, PBS and stations. We operate a  website  and publish a quarterly print publication. Our student reporters research, report and write their own stories with support from Current’s editors and staff reporters. Many have gone on to successful internships and professional jobs at other news organizations.  Essential Functions: Research, report and write original coverage. Gather information and multiple perspectives for news reporting through interviews, analysis, reading, observation and events. Check facts, spellings, numbers and assumptions to confirm details of news events. Produce timely and valuable material for digital coverage and report on developing stories. Revise work in progress and collaborate with editors in preparing coverage for online publication. Advise editors on art direction by collecting photos, artwork and graphics and identifying opportunities for presenting data and multimedia elements.   Work with Current staff on production, planning and discussion. Develop and pitch story ideas. Produce social media posts sharing links to Current’s news articles, adhering to Current’s editorial practices. Collaborate with digital editor and managing editor in responding to reader reactions. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 20 hours per week.   Salary Range:  $18.40 - $25.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: As of spring 2027, a junior, senior or graduate student with a major in American University's School of Communications. Minimum overall 3.25 GPA. Graduate students must have completed their first semester of study to be considered for this position.  Experience reporting for advanced SOC journalism courses. Analytical, quantitative and writing skills. Interest in journalism, public media, the media business and/or public policy. Preferred Education and Experience: Web publishing skills and familiarity with WordPress are preferred; however, we provide training for these skills as needed. Experience reporting in-depth stories or analyses for student journalism organizations or for previous editorial internships. Familiarity with the WordPress content management system. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Dates and hours: Jan. 11 – May 7, 2026; 20 hours per week (exact dates and daily work schedule to be worked out with supervisor). This internship is eligible for recognition by the  Dean's Internship program offered by American University's School of Communication.   Current operates as a virtual workplace.  To complete your application, upload your resume, three writing samples that best represent your work and a cover letter describing your qualifications and goals for the internship. Also provide contact information for three professors who we can contact as references. Contact Digital Editor Mike Janssen, mike@current.org with any questions. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Spring-Valley-Campus-Washington-DC/Program-Manager--Development---Innovation_R5080": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Development & Innovation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Research Integrity Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 02 (On Campus 2 days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Program Manager for Development and Innovation supports the university’s research enterprise by leading funding opportunity identification, faculty engagement, and innovation-support activities for the Office of Research and Sponsored Awards (ORSA). Under the VPRI’s direction, the position is responsible for proactively scanning federal and state agencies, foundations, and philanthropic organizations to identify emerging funding opportunities aligned with institutional research priorities. The Program Manager monitors sponsor trends and funding landscapes; curates targeted opportunities for faculty, research units, and other entities as assigned; maintains internal tracking systems; and coordinates the institution’s limited submission announcement process for competitive external funding.   Working closely with center directors, department leadership, and pre-award offices, as well as other entities as assigned, the Program Manager for Development and Innovation aligns research/program interests with suitable funding opportunities. Through intake consultations, opportunity matching, and improved communication across research and administrative units, the Program Manager supports entity preparedness and enhances proposal competitiveness across the university.   The role also contributes to the university’s innovation and technology transfer activities by partnering with technology transfer teams to identify opportunities for industry collaboration, commercialization potential, and innovation-focused programming. The Program Manager assists with workshops, pitch sessions, and partnership development activities; supports the evaluation of invention disclosures, emerging technologies, and social innovation; and contributes to responsibilities related to intellectual property, data infrastructure, and research security. The Program Manager will identify and engage with relevant parties across campus related to development and innovation, including but not limited to data infrastructure and security, tech transfer, translation of research, and other VRPI initiatives.   Overall, the Program Manager for Development and Innovation serves as a connector, advisor, and executor, supporting funding opportunity management, research/program development, and innovation activities to help build a dynamic, engaged, and supportive research environment.   Essential Functions: 1.)  Funding Strategy & Opportunity Management Conduct proactive scanning of federal agencies, foundations, and philanthropic organizations to identify emerging funding opportunities aligned with university research priorities. Monitor sponsor priorities, funding trends, and policy changes to inform strategic planning. Curate and distribute targeted funding opportunities to centers, departments, and faculty. Maintain and update internal tracking tools and databases; monitor deadlines, eligibility, and submission workflows. Partner with center directors, department leadership, and pre-award offices, as well as other entities as assigned, to align research/program interests with suitable funding opportunities. Conduct intake discussions with principal investigators (current and interested) to understand research needs and identify competitive funding pathways.                                                      2.) Intellectual Property Assist in assessment of new technologies, invention disclosures, and potential commercialization strategies. Manage intellectual property protection including patents and trademarks, including initial filing and maintenance. Ensure compliance with Bayh-Dole Act. Engage on-campus resources for intellectual property protection. Work closely with Director of Research Compliance and Integrity and the Office of General Counsel. Educate principal investigators (current and interested) and units on opportunities related to intellectual property.   3.) Innovation Partnerships & Technology Transfer Support Collaborate with technology transfer teams to identify opportunities for industry partnerships, commercialization, and innovation programming. Support innovation-related initiatives such as workshops, pitch sessions, and partnership development activities. Engage on-campus resources for entrepreneurship and technology transfer. Ensure compliance with Bayh-Dole Act.   4.) TRAC Management Portfolio Serve as the ORSA liaison to TRAC. Work with assessment team on development of AU capacity plan for technology transfer, intellectual property, and research translation support. Participate in regular TRAC meetings. Produce regular reports and updates to TRAC and ORSA. Identify opportunities for collaboration between TRAC, ORSA, and other entities across campus.   5.) Data Infrastructure & Security Coordinate data security and infrastructure plan development across campus. Identify relevant personnel and efforts across campus. Manage external partners in plan development and implementation. Produce data infrastructure and security enhancement report for VPRI and ensure the report is current.   Competencies: Developing Plans. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Prioritizing and Organizing. Displaying Creativity.  Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $80,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience.   Preferred Education and Experience: Master’s Degree or equivalent. 3 - 5 years of experience in related field.   Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Data-Quality-Assistant--Student-_R5103": {
      "title": "Data Quality Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Applications and Data Quality Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: AU’s Division of University Advancement (UA) supports the Office of Development by maintaining, providing, and improving the data, systems, and processes that fuel the University’s fundraising and advancement efforts. A critical member of the team, the Advancement Data Integrity Student Assistant is responsible for assisting Data Quality Associate Director and Project Manager by executing data cleaning, curation, mapping process, and documenting processes or/and training. Specific duties of the Student Assistant include, but are not limited to, managing the queue of incoming requests from university staff; providing support for data ingestion process, data cleansing, and monitoring; and assisting with business process analysis. Essential Functions: Maintaining, providing, and improving the data, systems, and processes that fuel the University’s fundraising and advancement efforts. Assisting Data Quality Associate Director and Project Manager by executing data cleaning, curation, mapping process, and documenting processes or/and training. Managing the queue of incoming requests from university staff. Providing support for data ingestion process, data cleansing, and monitoring. Assisting with business process analysis. Other duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 - 20 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 - $20.00 per hour. Required Education and Experienc e Strong skill with Microsoft Excel. Demonstrated skills in problem solving and paying attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal communication skills. Excellent organizational skills. Ability to work independently. Must be enrolled student at American University. Preferred Education and Experience Student studied in information technology, data science, related fields or experience. Familiarity with computer basics and word processing tools. Knowledge of SQL or programing/scripting languages. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: This position is currently 100% remote. It’s based on 4401 Connecticut Avenue NW. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Overnight-Desk-Assistant--Student-_R5089": {
      "title": "Overnight Desk Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Residence Life Training Leadership Programs Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary:   The Night Desk Assistant (NDA) is a part-time student staff member of Housing & Residence Life and a member of the University’s Division of Student Affairs.  The Night Desk Assistant fulfills a vital role in the residence hall system by helping ensure the safety of the halls, assisting residents with concerns, and welcoming guests and visitors. The Night Desk Assistant works exclusively during the hours of 11:00 PM – 7:00 AM.   The NDA is supervised by a Residential Operations Coordinator with the support from the Assistant Director for Residential Operations and Finance and is expected to work closely with other staff members (other DAs, Resident Assistants, Desk Coordinators, Community Directors, Facilities Management staff, etc.) within the building, as well as across campus.   Essential Functions:   1.) Administration Turn in completed HR and payroll forms to your supervisor or the Assistant Director for Residential Operations & Finance. Also, submit appropriate HR paperwork via Workday. Be timely and professional in all written and verbal communications with Housing & Residence Life staff and AU community members. Compile accurate and timely reports for supervisor as requested (shift logs, digital systems management). Complete and submit bi-weekly online timesheets on time via Workday. Treat information concerning staff and/or students with the utmost confidentiality. 2.) Community Facilitation and Customer Service Support efforts of front desk staff in creating a safe living environment for the residents. Answer questions from students, families, faculty, staff, prospective students, and alumni in person and over the phone. Follow proper protocol to check in and out guests of residents. Treat the concerns of all customers with attentiveness and seriousness. Maintain a working knowledge of the University’s facilities, services, and resources. Ensure that the desk is clean, all binders and logs are in appropriate locations, and all supplies are stocked. 3.) Role Modeling and Policy Compliance Monitor and enforce access to the residence hall. Be well versed in, personally abide by, and help enforce University policies including the Housing License Agreement.  NDAs must also abide by all regulations in federal and local jurisdictions. Confront, document, and follow through on violations of published University and Housing & Residence Life policies, regulations, and procedures in an accurate and timely manner. Abide by policies and procedures aligned in the protocol manual regarding building evacuations.   Understand that all actions of an NDA (including those engaged in outside of the residence hall) are observed by residents, other NDAs and staff members. 4.) Facilities/Operations Assist in the opening, closing, and staffing of the residence hall desks during University break times. Assist residents with checking in and out of their housing assignments using the StarRez housing assignment management software system. Follow lockout protocol to assist residents with regaining access to their rooms Create temporary access cards for residents that need them. Check out administrative keys to groups that have residence hall space reservations. Follow proper key distribution procedures to maintain accuracy and security. NDAs must not create or issue keys to anyone, including themselves, without following proper documentation procedures. 5.) Communication Maintain positive relationships with fellow Desk Assistants, Desk Coordinators, Resident Assistants, Community Directors, HRL staff, Facilities Management, and Program Associates. Participate in DA surveys to schedule desk shifts. Maintain ongoing communication with Residential Operations Coordinators, fellow Desk Assistants, and Housing & Residence Life office by checking phone messages and e-mail messages daily. Attend all scheduled shifts on time. Follow proper communication protocols when seeking emergency shift coverage.   Follow proper communication protocols when communicating with on-call staff and emergency personnel.   6.) Other duties as assigned: The nature of the NDA position does not allow for all duties to be explicitly described.  There will be times when hall staff are requested to assist in an emergency or other unforeseen circumstance.  These situations will be presented as thoroughly as possible at the time of need. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 8 - 24 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.60 per hour.   Required Education and Experience: Full time enrollment as an undergraduate  or graduate student at American University (minimum 12 credits and a maximum of 17 per semester). If a Desk Assistant wishes to drop below the minimum credit hours, they must receive written permission from the Director of Residence Life to retain the DA position. Cumulative GPA at, or above, 2.50 and term GPA at, or above, 2.50 (GPAs must be maintained from the date of application until the date of separation). Must be in good conduct standing with the university. Participate in the Desk Assistant interview process.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: This is a 10-month position from August through May. All Night Desk Assistants must attend and fully participate in staff training in August and January prior to the start of the academic semester. All Night Desk Assistants are expected to work during the opening of residence halls. The residential front desks at American University are a 24-hour operation throughout the entire academic year. This position works during the hours of 11:00 PM-7:00 AM only.  Night Desk Assistants are expected to work a minimum of 8 hours (maximum 24 hours) per week, including some weekend shifts. Night Desk Assistants are expected to be available to work both the 11:00pm-3:00am and 3:00am- 7:00am shift options each weeks. Night Desk Assistants are required to work one break (Thanksgiving Break, Winter Early Arrival, a portion of Spring Break) over the course of the academic year. Night Desk Assistants are required to work during Finals and hall closing periods. Desk Assistants (Day), and Desk Coordinators are not eligible to serve as Night Desk Assistants. Staff are required to be present and participate in all DA training and residence hall opening and closing dates. All dates are subject to change. Applicants are required to attend one Desk Assistant information session. Qualifying candidates will be required to answer additional supplemental questions after applications close. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/WCL-Graduate-Admissions-Assistant--Student-_R5090": {
      "title": "WCL Graduate Admissions Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Graduate Admissions Assistant supports the LL.M. and SJD Programs admissions functions by providing support for general office tasks and communications. This includes assisting with data entry, follow up communication, creation of documents for meetings and applicant files, maintaining and directing mail, managing social media, and other miscellaneous administrative tasks. This position requires attention to detail and strong communication skills. This position will report directly to the Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions. This position will interact with many people on a daily basis ranging from students (around 200) and prospective students (around 800), professors, administrators, and professionals from the community. As a vital addition to the staff, this position will support and ensure that the Graduate Admissions Office is able to maintain the level of student services necessary to maintain and grow enrollment numbers. Essential Functions: File Maintenance: Create application files, track completion requirements, communicate application status to students, approve submitted application materials, transition files for review, and close files as necessary. Data Entry: Maintain accurate records for individual applicants. Track applicant status in Salesforce and LSAC. General Clerical: Answers the main telephone line. Directs telephone calls and walk-ins to the proper channels. Maintain the general admissions email inbox. Respond to general applicant questions via email or directing them to the correct point of contact. Social Media: Manage the Instagram account for LL.M. admissions. Publish videos and posts that assist with recruitment. Work with the Assistant Director to support the overall marketing strategy. Other duties as assigned. Graduate Admissions Assistant can suggest additional projects of interest. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: We cannot consider current WCL LL.M. students for this position. Must be an AU graduate student and does not qualify for visa sponsorship or OPT. Completed bachelor’s degree or equivalent. Proficiency in Microsoft Outlook, Excel, and Word is required. Preferred Education and Experience: Experience with social media is preferred. At least two years of office experience and/or in a university/ law office is preferred. Knowledge of databases such as Salesforce is helpful. Professional-level Spanish proficiency is preferred. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Industry-Engagement-Specialist_R4862": {
      "title": "Industry Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Kogod School of Business Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 02 (On Campus 2 days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Industry Engagement Specialist (IES) spearheads establishing and maintaining robust partnerships with key players in [specific industry, e.g., finance, technology, healthcare, sustainability, consulting, media, entertainment, hospitality, real estate] to cultivate new employer relationships for the purpose of enhancing career outcomes for Kogod undergraduate and graduate students. The IES will expand internship and job opportunities for Kogod students by establishing strong relationships with key employers, recruiters, and alumni in order to develop important networks, identify quality internship and career programs and opportunities, and keep abreast of employer needs. The IES will identify and build relationships with target employers within the specified key industry sector with strong internship and full-time job opportunities that align with Kogod students’ interests and strengths, and to increase opportunities for students to interview with these companies by effectively marketing the Kogod School of Business. The successful candidate will be responsible for identifying potential corporate partners, developing engagement strategies, coordinating recruitment events, and ensuring a continuous presence of industry opportunities available to our students. This position demands a proactive approach, excellent relationship-building skills, and a deep understanding of industry trends to effectively match our students' skills with employer needs. The IES will act as a bridge between the business school and industry, enhancing the school's reputation as a prime source of top-tier talent. Essential Functions: 1.) Outreach and Engagement Develop a strategic vision and plan for ongoing engagement with external partners, including employers and alumni, and oversee execution of that plan throughout the calendar year. Understand Needs of Employer: Conduct research to understand the industries, sectors, and types of organizations that are of interest to students. Gather feedback from employers about their recruitment needs, competition, challenges facing the company, preferred communication channels, and expectations. Gain deep understanding of student populations and curricular highlights to be able to market Kogod student and alumni talent. Listen to what employers want and key obstacles or barriers to success. Attend networking functions as appropriate to develop employer contacts while promoting university and college objectives. Build and Maintain Relationships: Create, cultivate, and maintain external relationships to ensure active engagement; establish personal connections with employer representatives. Regularly communicate with employers to stay updated on their recruitment needs, upcoming opportunities, and feedback on student candidates. Maintain communication to ensure awareness and create a regular cadence for outreach. Foster long-term relationships by providing value added services and meeting needs. Develop Targeted Engagement Strategy: Prioritize employers based on their potential to offer valuable opportunities to students and their willingness to engage with Kogod. Create a plan for outreach and engagement tailored to the specific needs of the employer. Conduct business development, both virtually and in person, within industries including outreach to new companies and increasing the Kogod hiring footprint across companies where relationships currently exist. Understand the unique recruitment challenges and objectives of each employer and tailor services accordingly. Understand recruiting timelines to ensure deliverables meet expectations. Promote ethical standards such as interviewing protocols. 2.) Collaboration with Career Coaches, Faculty and Staff  Meet regularly with career coaches to share information about employer events, recruiting opportunities, application deadlines, etc. Work with career coaches to identify students for key opportunities and inclusion in curated resume books. Collaborate with UG, MBA, and specialty master’s program faculty to better understand curriculum and share insights into how curriculum can support employer needs. Share information with faculty and program leadership about specific opportunities, events, and application deadlines. Share industry and recruiting insights with faculty and program leadership. 3.) Special Programming Participate in the design and plan of strategic engagements such as career fairs, networking events, etc. for Kogod and American University.  Offer Customized Solutions: Provide solutions such as fairs, networking events, employer panels, and industry-specific workshops etc. to facilitate interactions between students and employers. Partner with student clubs to deliver targeted engagements and enhance connectivity. Provide customized recruitment solutions such as career sessions, coffee chats, in class presentations, skills sessions, site visits, 1:1 or group engagements – both in-person and virtual. Partnerships: Partners with departments and other academic units to identify relevant and appropriate on-campus professional development opportunities, including class speakers, panelists, and career mentoring opportunities; works with event staff to ensure positive experience for students and guests. 4.) Communication, Databases, and Reporting Contribute to and maintain a database of active employers and alumni and reports on engagement activities, their success, and recommendations for future opportunities.   Communication: Create content on appropriate media channels to maximize visibility of opportunities both to promote beforehand and report on afterwards.  CRM: Maintain accurate notes on employer outreach and engagement; prepare correspondence, reports, and presentations regarding outreach activities and events; track communication to ensure successful activities and events are documented.  Evaluate Effort: Utilize key performance indicators (KPIs) as established by leadership to measure effectiveness of employer engagement efforts. Regularly assess the impact of engagement activities on student outcomes, employer satisfaction, and overall career services objectives. Participate in semester and year end debrief meetings as well and contribute to reporting. Use feedback from employers and students to continuously improve engagement strategies and services offered.  Outcomes: Collaborate with data team to collect and track student outcomes from employers and maintain knowledge of applicable reporting standards.  Stay Informed: Stay updated on industry trends, participate in professional development workshops, conferences, and training sessions, and implement new strategies or techniques learned.    5.) Industry-Specific Guidance and Other Duties Training: Share industry trends, recruiting timelines, and other best practices with coaching teams and staff to inform student preparation. Participate in development of student resources related to industry trends and hiring timelines. Other duties as assigned: Facilitate special projects, serve on committees, etc. as needed. Competencies: Serving Customers. Displaying Creativity.   Prioritizing and Organizing. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Supporting Coworkers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. The schedule is 9AM - 5PM, Monday - Friday with some evening/weekend hours. Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $85,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent.  4 - 6 years of relevant experience. Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree or equivalent. 5 - 8 years of relevant experience. Travel Required: Position requires domestic and international travel. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: 1.) Values and Approach  Team Orientation: Collaborate effectively and communicate transparently while welcoming diverse viewpoints.   Quality Focus: Consistently produce accurate and exceptional work in dynamic environment.   Initiative and Ingenuity: Generate innovative ways to create and implement ideas.   Continuous Learning: Maintain an optimistic outlook and adaptable approach to work.   Inclusive Leadership: Inspire and motivate others to meet goals while providing clarity and empathy.   2.) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficient communication skill. Experience and knowledge of, or demonstrated interest in, business careers. Demonstrated knowledge of relationship management databases. High proficiency in MS Office, including Excel and PowerPoint along with demonstrated in-depth experience using LinkedIn and other professional social networking sites. Experience in University career services, recruiting, staffing, human resources or business development. 3.) Preferred Skills Broad understanding of the value of a business school education, particularly MBA and specialty master's programs and the international visa process. Experience in or knowledge of working within industry specific areas. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Spring-Valley-Campus-Washington-DC/Information-Security-Architect_R5075": {
      "title": "Information Security Architect",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Information Security Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 04 (On Campus 1 day/Month) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Information Security Architect serves as the university’s senior technical security architect and a key advisor on enterprise security strategy, architecture, and engineering. Reporting to the Chief Information Security Officer, this role leads the design and integration of security controls across a complex technology environment, including cloud platforms, infrastructure, identity, applications, and research computing. The position partners closely with technical and business stakeholders to ensure security is embedded into solutions by design, aligned with institutional priorities, risk management objectives, and regulatory requirements. This role also drives security engineering innovation through automation, Infrastructure as Code, DevSecOps, and platform integration. The architect provides leadership on security reviews, technical standards, and emerging technology assessments while mentoring engineering staff and helping strengthen the overall maturity of the university’s security program.   Essential Functions: 1.) Security Architecture and Technical Governance Develop and maintain enterprise security architectures, reference architectures, and design patterns that integrate security into technology solutions by design. Lead architecture and security design reviews for infrastructure, cloud, networking, identity, data, and application initiatives. Establish technical security standards and requirements for technology procurement, implementation, and enterprise initiatives. Ensure security architecture aligns with university objectives, risk tolerance, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices. 2.) Security Engineering, Automation, and Platform Strategy Design and implement automation solutions using APIs, orchestration technologies, scripting languages, and Infrastructure as Code. Define engineering standards, reusable patterns, and technical roadmaps for enterprise security platforms. Lead integration efforts between security and enterprise technology platforms. Guide adoption of automation, DevSecOps, and Infrastructure as Code practices across the Information Security program. 3.) Security Reviews, Risk Assessment, and Advisory Services Lead security assessments of university technologies, cloud services, applications, vendors, and third-party solutions. Evaluate security risks associated with strategic initiatives and recommend mitigation strategies. Provide technical security guidance to project teams, architects, engineers, and university leadership. Participate in Enterprise Architecture activities and strategic technology planning. Support compliance, audit, privacy, and regulatory initiatives through architecture and technical review activities. 4.) Security Program Leadership and Engineering Enablement Mentor and provide technical guidance to Security Engineers and Senior Security Engineers, building team capability and depth. Establish security engineering implementation guidance and operational best practices. Support roadmap development and security program planning. Contribute to development of security metrics, reporting, and maturity assessments. 5.) Research, Innovation, and Emerging Technology Evaluate emerging technologies, threats, and security trends, including the security roadmaps of major enterprise platforms such as Microsoft, Workday, Salesforce, and ServiceNow. Assess opportunities to improve security through automation, AI, analytics, and engineering innovation. Recommend improvements to university security capabilities and long-term technology strategy. Participate in professional organizations, industry working groups, and technical communities. Competencies: Serving Customers. Displaying Creativity. Prioritizing and Organizing. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Supporting Coworkers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. This position works Monday through Friday with a one-hour lunch break in a hybrid modality with one day a month required to work from the office. This position participates in a published on-call rotation, typically one week out of every four weeks, with more frequent rotations possible during staffing shortages or unplanned absences. Purpose of on-call rotation: The Information Security on-call rotation ensures timely detection, response, and coordination for security alerts and incidents that occur outside of standard business hours. This rotation is a critical operational responsibility of Information Security staff and supports the institution’s overall risk-management and incident-response obligations. During an on-call rotation, the designated employee performs their regularly work duties and must be readily available throughout the day (including evenings, weekends, and holidays) to proactively monitor alerts, queues and dashboards and respond to incidents. Outside of on-call rotations, all team members are expected to be reasonably available to respond to emergencies and critical or time-sensitive security incidents. This role may require frequent interrupted nights and weekends. The on-call designee will be required to work remotely, during unplanned closures or weather emergencies. The rest of the team is expected to be on call and available to work remotely to address emergency IT issues. OIT staff are prohibited from taking non-emergency leave during the three-week period at the start of each semester, this includes the week before the start of the Fall and Spring term and the first two weeks of classes for the Fall and Spring term. Requests for support peak during these times and system availability is also critical, which requires all staff members to be working during these times.  Salary Range: $150,000.00 - $160,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 8 - 10 years of experience. Preferred Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree. Experience working in higher education or similarly complex, decentralized organizations is preferred. Relevant industry certifications such as CISSP, CCSP, GIAC, AWS Security Specialty, Azure Security Engineer Associate, Terraform Associate, or equivalent certifications are preferred.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. 8 - 10 years of experience in cybersecurity, systems engineering, cloud engineering, DevSecOps, infrastructure engineering, or related disciplines. Demonstrated experience designing, implementing, and maintaining enterprise security architectures in complex organizations. Extensive experience with AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform. Experience with Infrastructure as Code and automation technologies, including Terraform, OpenTofu, CloudFormation, Bicep, Ansible, Git, CI/CD platforms, and scripting languages such as Python, PowerShell, or Bash. Experience integrating enterprise platforms through APIs, automation frameworks, orchestration tools, and workflow development. Experience with security operations, including detection engineering, security automation, and Security Orchestration Automation and Response (SOAR) platforms. Experience designing secure research, regulated, or high-assurance computing environments. Experience with enterprise security technologies, security engineering practices, and modern cloud-native security controls. Knowledge of security standards and frameworks including NIST, ISO 27001, FERPA, HIPAA, and higher education security practices. Excellent technical, analytical, problem-solving, written and verbal communication skills. Must uphold high standards of personal and professional integrity in a position of trust. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/4401-Connecticut-Campus-Washington-DC/Senior-Director-of-Executive-Engagement_R5077-1": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Executive Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: WAMU Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: WAMU 88.5 is a public media station owned and operated by American University. WAMU is the source for local, regional and NPR news and original programs in Washington DC. Since 1961, WAMU has been amplifying voices and sharing stories from the many neighborhoods and communities in the District of Columbia, Maryland and Virginia. The Senior Director of Executive Engagement partners with the General Manager and senior leadership to develop  and execute executive engagement and messaging strategies that strengthen  the GM’s effectiveness and influence across internal and external audiences. This role serves as a trusted strategic advisor to the GM, leading executive communications, stakeholder engagement, governance support, and high profile institutional engagements. The position ensures a coordinated and strategic approach to executive relationships and communications, manages the GM’s Executive Assistant and may lead additional staff, serving as a trusted advisor and connector across the organization.  Essential Functions:    1.) Strategic Communications Develop executive messaging strategies and communication frameworks that support the General Manager’s priorities and organizational objectives.   Develop and oversee drafting of speeches, op-eds, and executive correspondence, presentations, talking points and briefing materials.  Ensure consistency and alignment of executive communications with organizational priorities and institutional messaging.  Collaborate with Advancement on executive communications supporting major donor communication and relationship management.  Collaborate with Marketing to position the GM as a thought leader and representative of WAMU and public media.  Partner with Communications, Marketing and Advancement to ensure coordinated executive messaging across internal and external audiences.  Support strategic partnerships and manage external executive speaking engagements.  Prepare the General Manager and other senior leaders, as appropriate, for impactful representation of the WAMU brand at external engagements, interviews, and public appearances.   2.) Executive Engagement & Stakeholder Management Develop and execute strategies that strengthen the General Manager’s engagement with the Board of Advisors, Community Council, American University leadership, Trustees, donors, community leaders, and external industry partners.   Develop executive engagement strategies that prepare the GM for high impact interactions with internal and external stakeholders.   Develop messaging and engagement plans for executive led forums, including All Staff meetings, to effectively communicate organizational priorities and foster transparency.   Advise the GM on executive communications and stakeholder engagement approaches that align with organizational priorities.   Lead preparation for the General Manager’s participation in high impact internal and external engagements, including briefing materials, messaging, and stakeholder strategies.   Develop and maintain executive stakeholder engagement plans and relationship maps for AU leadership, Trustees, the Board of Advisors, Community Council, donors, and other key constituents.   Represent the GM in select external interactions, as appropriate.    3.) Board Relations & Governance Serve as the General Manager’s strategic advisor on Board engagement, shaping meeting objectives, discussion topics, and communications to strengthen relationships with the Board of Advisors, Community Council, and American University Trustees.   Manage the cadence of Board communications, reporting and governance activities between meetings ensuring timely preparation of materials and follow up on Board actions. Lead development and coordination of Board and committee agendas, briefing materials, presentations, reports, and meeting documentation.   Ensure timely and accurate reporting aligned with governance standards and Board reporting requirements.  Coordinate delivery of any WAMU materials as needed by AU Trustees, the Board of Advisors, and Community Council.  Oversee planning and execution of Board meetings, retreats, and other Board related events. including preparation of executive agendas, briefing materials, and stakeholder communications.     4.) Team Leadership & Operations Manage the GM’s Senior Executive Assistant.  Set priorities, coach for performance, and ensure seamless executive support.  Partner with senior leaders to coordinate executive priorities, facilitate follow through on General Manager commitments, and ensure alignment across the Office of the GM and organizational goals.  Supervisory Responsibility: Supervises the Senior Executive Assistant. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week.  Hybrid work modality (3 - 4 days per week in office).  Salary Range: $140,000.00 - $155,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: ​​Bachelor's degree or equivalent​. ​​8 - 10 years of relevant experience​.   Preferred Education and Experience: ​​Master's degree​. ​​10+ years of relevant experience​.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in communications, Business Administration, or related field; advanced degree preferred.  8 - 10 years of experience in executive communications, stakeholder engagement, or strategic operations.  Demonstrated ability to lead projects and people while influencing senior stakeholders.  Exceptional writing, presentation, and relationship management abilities (strong interpersonal skills). Strong strategic thinking combined with operational execution skills (ability to identify trends and patterns and connect dots).   Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.  Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/4401-Connecticut-Campus-Washington-DC/Senior-Director-of-Strategic-Operations_R5078": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Strategic Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Operations Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: WAMU 88.5 is a public media station owned and operated by American University. WAMU is the source for local, regional and NPR news and original programs in Washington DC. Since 1961, WAMU has been amplifying voices and sharing stories from the many neighborhoods and communities in the District of Columbia, Maryland and Virginia.   The Senior Director of Strategic Operations serves as a strategic advisor and operational partner to the Chief Operating Officer, advancing the COO's strategic priorities by establishing the operating cadence, planning frameworks, and performance standards that guide execution across WAMU. Under the direction of the COO, the role works with senior leaders and their organizations to build alignment, implement consistent operating practices, and ensure enterprise initiatives are executed with accountability and measurable results. Through influence, collaboration, and independent judgment, the Director strengthens organizational effectiveness without assuming operational ownership of functional departments.  Essential Functions:    1.) Drive Enterprise Initiatives  Lead development and execution of enterprise wide strategic initiatives tied to the Operating Plan, advising executive leadership on priorities, sequencing, organizational risks and resource requirements.(e.g., data framework development, technology modernization, enterprise onboarding).  Partner with executive leadership to translate organizational strategy into enterprise execution plans, defining priorities, success measures, governance, accountability, and organizational outcomes. Translate strategic goals into actionable plans.  Define scope, success metrics, sponsors, DRIs (directly responsible individuals), stakeholders, and contributors.  Partner with initiative sponsors and leaders to maintain focus, anticipate challenges, and ensure delivery milestones are met.  Recommend strategic solutions to complex organizational challenges and advise executive leadership on emerging risks, opportunities, and competing priorities.   2.) Establish a Unified Execution Framework Design, implement, and continuously improve the enterprise framework governing strategic initiatives, organizational priorities, and interdependencies.   Establish enterprise standards and governance practices for defining, prioritizing, launching, and monitoring strategic initiatives.   Coach WAMU leaders and initiative sponsors in applying enterprise planning disciplines, risk management, and organizational accountability practices.     3.) Orchestrate the Operating Rhythm Lead the organization’s operating rhythm, including enterprise planning, quarterly business reviews, annual planning, executive reporting, and strategic decision support.   Develop executive decision-support materials that synthesize organizational performance, risks, resource needs, and strategic opportunities.  Influence and align executive leaders across Finance, Technology, Advancement, People & Culture, and Content to ensure enterprise priorities are integrated, appropriately resourced, and aligned with organizational strategy.    4.) Enable Collaboration and Accountability Serve as a trusted advisor to executive leadership, influencing alignment across organizational priorities, governance, and strategic decision making.  Lead resolution of highly complex cross-functional issues requiring executive judgment, organizational consensus, and strategic tradeoff decisions.  Build organizational capability by coaching leaders in strategic execution, accountability, and enterprise collaboration.    5.) Measure and Improve Performance Develop the organization's enterprise performance framework, recommending organizational metrics that inform executive decision making and long-term strategic planning.  Identify systemic organizational risks, emerging trends, operational opportunities, and recommend executive actions to improve organizational effectiveness.  Lead continuous improvement efforts that strengthen enterprise operating practices, organizational effectiveness, and strategic execution.    Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week  Hybrid work modality (3 - 4 days per week in office). Salary Range: $140,000.00 - $155,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: ​​Bachelor's degree or equivalent​.   ​​8 - 10 years of relevant experience​.   Preferred Education and Experience: ​​Master's degree​. ​​10+ years of relevant experience​.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: 10+ years of experience in operations, enterprise initiative management, or strategic project leadership.  Demonstrated success advising executive leadership and leading enterprise-wide strategic initiatives that require influence across multiple functions without direct authority.  Expertise in project and portfolio management tools (Asana, Smartsheet, Monday, or similar).  Strong analytical and synthesis skills; able to translate complexity into clear, actionable plans.  Exceptional communication, facilitation, and executive presentation abilities.  Adept at balancing strategic thinking with tactical execution.    Other Duties:   Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.  Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Graduate-Career-Outcomes-and-Assessment-Assistant--Student-_R5084": {
      "title": "Graduate Career Outcomes and Assessment Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Career Operations, Data & Systems Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: This position coordinates administrative functions supporting the annual Graduation Census and academic internship programs in the Career Center at American University.   The Assistant works to improve Graduation Census knowledge and response rates and internship evaluation response rates by conducting research and connecting with AU students, faculty, recent alumni, and select external audiences to collect Graduation Census data and internship evaluations.  The Career Outcomes and Assessment Assistant will jointly report to the Director of Employer Relations & External Partnerships and the Director of Operations, Data, & Systems in the AU Career Center, and may supervise the work of one student assistant each semester.  Essential Functions:  Conduct research and targeted outreach to recent bachelor’s and master’s graduates to support Graduation Census response goals.  Record, review, and validate the Graduation Census and internship evaluation data, ensuring accuracy and completeness.  Create, maintain, and update detailed tracking systems, documents, and status reports.   Support outreach to students, faculty, alumni, and external partners related to academic internship evaluations and other assessment efforts.  Monitor and triage survey-related email correspondence, prepare responses, and refer inquiries to appropriate Career Center colleagues.  Maintain privacy and confidentiality and follow established data governance practices when handling student, alumni, employer, and survey information.  Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 12 - 15 hours per week.   Salary Range: $20.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Must be currently enrolled in a graduate program at American University.  At least one year of relevant experience in a professional office setting.  Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, contact management systems, and social media platforms, particularly LinkedIn.  Demonstrated ability to learn and navigate systems and follow established processes.  Excellent written and verbal communication skills.  Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and maintain accurate records.  Demonstrated initiative and the ability to work independently, meet deadlines, and achieve established goals.  Preferred Education and Experience:  Familiarity with Handshake  and an online survey tool (e.g., SurveyMonkey,  Qualtrics, CVENT/Inquisium). Familiarity with career services programs and operations in a higher education setting. Additional Eligibility Qualifications:  This is a part-time contract position beginning in October 2026 and ending in April 2027.   We highly recommend attaching a resume and cover letter to the submitted online application.  Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
