    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/4401-Connecticut-Campus-Washington-DC/Senior-Administrative-Assistant_R4559": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Alumni Relations Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: The Senior Administrative Assistant will provide administrative support in the Division of University Advancement, primarily assisting the Assistant Vice President of Alumni Relations (AVP) as well as other staff members as directed by the AVP. In their work, the Senior Administrative Assistant will enhance alumni relations programs and volunteer initiatives that increase alumni engagement within the 160,000+ member AU alumni network. Responsibilities include but are not limited to processing mail; answering phones; scheduling meetings; appointments and travel (including arrangements); transcribing correspondence and phone outreach to constituents; organizing and maintaining filing systems; assisting with events; and other meetings held by the AVP; making on-campus deliveries or pick-ups of materials; reconciling credit card transactions of the AVP; conducting basic research (for names, phone numbers and addresses); and producing mailings and meeting materials. In addition, the Senior Administrative Assistant will draft internal and external correspondence. The Senior Administrative Assistant will interact with senior administrators, alumni, volunteers, and donors to the University. Essential Functions: 1.) General Administrative Duties Assists with events, schedules meetings and appointments, maintains travel calendar for the AVP. Processes mail, answers phones and personal and shared email inboxes, makes on-campus deliveries. Conducts basic desktop research including names, phone numbers, addresses, career and degree info. Reconciles credit card transactions for the AVP. Drafts internal and external emails and other correspondence, produces mailings and meeting materials. 2.) Volunteer Management and Logistics Manage the logistics and communications for four quarterly AU Alumni Board (AUAB) meetings including space reservation, catering, and preparations of materials. Manage logistics and communications for annual AUAB new member orientation. Interact with AUAB members to schedule phone calls, committee meetings, ensure participation, send reminders, etc. Maintain and update current rosters AUAB and other alumni relations volunteer leadership groups. Provide secondary support for other alumni relations volunteer leadership groups including those in the Mosaic Collective, career, enrollment, and regional chapters. 3.) Data Management and Reporting Updates records in the Ellucian CRM Advance database including contact reports, engagement, biographical and demographic data. Prioritizes data hygiene and organization to ensure that engagement activities, event lists, and lists of alumni volunteer leaders and interested alums are kept up to date in the CRM . Utilizes CRM and MicroStrategy business intelligence reports and dashboards to support the AVPs, alumni relations directors, and other UA and AU leaders in employing a data-driven approach to evaluating and refining alumni engagement programs and activities.             4.) Volunteer Engagement and Stewardship Support the division’s goals to increase alumni engagement through volunteer management by managing volunteer stewardship projects including, but not limited to: monthly congratulations letters, birthday and anniversary mailings and emails to volunteer leaders, and frequent direct outreach to volunteer leaders, coordinating AVP, VP, and alumni relations directors’ direct outreach to volunteer leaders, compiling and distributing relevant content for volunteer leaders’ benefit, and regular audits of volunteer coding in the CRM. 5.) Other Duties as Assigned Supervisory Responsibility: This position may supervise student and/or part-time staff. Competencies: Serving Customers. Prioritizing and Organizing. Supporting Coworkers. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Championing Customer Needs. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Availability to work some nights and weekends. Salary Range: $26.11 - $28.87 per hour. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent. A minimum of 1 - 3 years of successful experience in alumni, donor, or community relations for educational  institutions or non-profit organizations. Ability to independently formulate long-range objectives, and manage varied programs and services Ability to set priorities, meet deadlines and work independently. Demonstrated organizational and decision-making skills with follow-up abilities. Mature and professional attitude, customer/client focus; highly developed interpersonal skills; energetic and detail oriented. Clear, concise reporting and writing style Computer literacy, particularly MS Word and Excel. Preferred Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience. At least one year of experience in volunteer management. Training and/or experience managing community initiatives and/or programs preferred. Intercultural communication skills or a level of intercultural competence preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Adjunct-Faculty---CAS-Department-of-Economics_R951-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - CAS Department of Economics (Open Continuous)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Exempt Job Description: This is an open continuous vacancy announcement that will be used to fill adjunct vacancies as they occur. Until you hear from a representative of the Department of Economics or the Office of HR Faculty, please continue to also apply directly to other positions posted on AU's website. The Department of Economics in the College of Arts and Sciences at American University invites applications for a number of adjunct faculty positions for upcoming Academic Years. Rank will depend on an applicant’s highest degree earned in Economics or a closely related field. The applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The Department of Economics offers both undergraduate and graduate degree programs. The Department is organized under the College of Arts and Sciences, which is where scholarship in the Arts, Humanities, and Sciences is pursued. Learn more about the College of Arts and Sciences at https://www.american.edu/cas/ and the Department of Economics at https://www.american.edu/cas/economics/ . The Department of Economics in the College of Arts and Sciences has the following adjunct salary ranges: Candidates Without a Terminal Degree In Course Subject Area 1-2 Credit Course: $2,865 3-4 Credit Course: $4,725 5-6 Credit Course: $4,938 Candidates With a Terminal Degree In Course Subject Area 1-2 Credit Course: $3,414 3-4 Credit Course: $5,400 5-6 Credit Course: $5,548 Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
