    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Imagery-Analysis-Research-Assistant---Student-_R5120-1": {
      "title": "Imagery Analysis Research Assistant  (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: Prof Alonzo seeks multiple research assistants to work on a project trying to understand the proliferation of solar pv technology in the Middle East. This project makes use of 30 cm resolution satellite imagery from 2021 and 2025 over Lebanon and Jordan. The main job is to help train and validate deep learning, computer vision models tasked with locating and measuring solar panels.   Essential Functions: Annotate the locations and sizes of solar panel arrays in Jordan and Lebanon on high-resolution satellite imagery. Assist in training and validation of deep learning models for solar panel location. Train others in online annotation workflows.  Other tasks on this project as requested. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 5 - 8 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Start and end date: October 10, 2026 – May 15, 2027. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Research-Assistant--NSF-Methane-Cycle--Student-_R5119-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, NSF Methane Cycle (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The research assistant will assist with data analysis related to an NSF-funded project on understanding the role of trees in the global methane cycle. Specifically, they will use R to clean up a large data set of methane emissions from baldcypress trees, estimate missing values, determine how methane fluxes vary in time and space, and extrapolate point measurements to an entire forest plot. The research assistant will also be involved in creating figures and tables and writing text for a scientific manuscript arising from this research. Essential Functions: Meet weekly with Karen Knee and Betty Malloy to discuss progress and update goals. Clean up data set to remove points that result from measurement error and estimate missing values. Create graphs and tables using R and R studio to visualize the data. Use statistical and data analysis methods to characterize how tree gas fluxes vary in time (different months of the year) and space (different trees and height on tree stem). Use point measurements to generate plot- and forest-scale gas flux estimates. Generate figures, tables, and text for a scientific publication. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 5 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
