    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Integrated-Marketing-Project-Manager_R4963": {
      "title": "Integrated Marketing Project Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: School of Public Affairs Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Integrated Marketing Project Manager will work closely with SPA’s Director of Marketing to develop, execute, and optimize integrated marketing campaigns that advance organizational goals and effectively engage target audiences. This role supports the development of  campaign strategy from concept through completion, and will translate institutional priorities into data-informed marketing initiatives across multiple channels. The Integrated Marketing Manager will also collaborate with SPA’s larger Communications & Marketing team to produce compelling content, ensure consistent brand messaging, and deliver high-quality campaigns on time and within budget. By monitoring performance metrics and analyzing results, the Integrated Marketing Project Manager drives continuous improvement, strengthens return on investment, and support the development of strategic insights to leadership to inform future marketing efforts. Essential Functions: 1.) Campaign Strategy and Planning Support the development and implementation of integrated marketing campaigns that align with organizational priorities and target audience needs. Collaborate with marketing leadership to define campaign objectives, key performance indicators, messaging, and audience targeting strategies. Conduct market research, gather institutional data, and help translate strategic goals into actionable campaign plans. Assist with timeline development, resource coordination, and campaign planning to support successful execution. 2.) Campaign Execution and Project Management Manage the day-to-day execution of marketing campaigns, ensuring deliverables are completed on time and aligned with established goals. Coordinate with internal stakeholders, creative partners, digital teams, and external vendors to support workflow and project progress. Monitor campaign activities, identify and address challenges, and help maintain consistency in messaging, branding, and overall campaign quality across platforms. 3.) Content and Creative Direction Collaborate closely with the SPA Comms team and other stakeholders to produce campaign content and creative assets across digital channels, including graphics, short-form videos, email content, and social media assets. Provide creative direction and feedback while designing, editing, and optimizing assets as needed to support campaign goals. Ensure all deliverables maintain a high standard of quality, consistency, and effectiveness. 4.) Channel Strategy and Optimization Support the implementation and management of campaign activities across digital, social media, email, web, and other appropriate channels. Assist in deploying campaign assets, monitoring channel performance, and recommending adjustments to improve engagement and reach. Apply best practices and emerging trends to optimize campaign effectiveness. 5.) Performance Measurement and Analytics Track and evaluate campaign performance using established metrics and reporting tools. Analyze engagement, conversion, and other performance data to identify trends and opportunities for improvement. Prepare reports and dashboards that communicate results and support data-informed decision-making by marketing leadership. 6.) Stakeholder Communication and Compliance Maintain regular communication with internal stakeholders to provide updates on campaign progress and outcomes. Support alignment with organizational priorities and help respond to evolving needs. Ensure marketing activities adhere to institutional policies, brand standards, accessibility requirements, and other relevant guidelines. 7.) Other Duties as Assigned Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Hybrid 1 work modality (3 - 4 days per week on campus). Salary Range: $72,500.00 - $75,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, or a related field required. 3 - 5 years progressively responsible experience in marketing, campaign management, or a related field. Experience managing multi-channel marketing campaigns and working within a collaborative team environment. Preferred Education and Experience: Master’s degree in a related field preferred (may be substituted with additional relevant experience). Experience with marketing analytics tools, CRM systems, or marketing automation platforms preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Demonstrated knowledge of marketing principles, campaign strategy development, and audience segmentation. Strong project management skills with the ability to manage multiple campaigns simultaneously and meet deadlines. Ability to analyze data, interpret performance metrics, and translate insights into actionable strategies. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to develop and refine messaging for diverse audiences. Proficiency in digital marketing channels, including email marketing, social media, web content, and paid media. Ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and external vendors. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage complex workflows. Knowledge of branding principles and experience maintaining consistent brand standards. Ability to manage budgets and allocate resources efficiently. Strategic thinking skills, with the ability to align marketing efforts with broader organizational goals. Adaptability and initiative to respond to changing priorities and emerging marketing trends. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Spring-Valley-Campus-Washington-DC/Program-Coordinator--AU-Abroad_R4837": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, AU Abroad",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Operations Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: Reporting to the Director of Operations, the Program Coordinator supports the advancement of the university’s Global Pledge by strengthening the systems, data, and communications that enable increased student participation in global experiences. The position plays a central role in the management of AU Abroad’s digital and operational infrastructure, with primary responsibility for Terra Dotta (CMS and website), data integrity, and reporting that informs recruitment, retention, and strategic planning efforts. Through accessible, student‑centered communications; coordinated data and operational workflows; and timely analysis and reporting, the Program Coordinator plays an active role in shaping positive student experiences across the full lifecycle of global programs. The position supports recruitment for global opportunities, promotes student engagement and persistence, and contributes to retention by ensuring clear guidance, proactive outreach, and responsive operational support. Working collaboratively with campus partners, the role connects systems, communications, and day‑to‑day operations to institutional priorities for global engagement and student success, while exercising independent judgment, professionalism, and strong project management skills. Essential Functions:   1.) Data and Reporting Coordinate with campus partners—including the Career Center, SIS Abroad, and the Kogod Global Learning Office—to collect and consolidate comprehensive data on student participation in global experiences. Analyze, synthesize, and distribute data related to the university’s Global Pledge, producing reports used by AU Abroad leadership and university administration to assess progress toward strategic goals. Identify and present trends, gaps, and opportunities in student participation data to inform recruitment, access, and retention strategies. Prepare and submit AU’s global mobility data for external reporting, including the Institute of International Education’s annual Open Doors report. 2.) Database and Website Management Serve as the primary liaison between AU Abroad and the Terra Dotta vendor, managing system requests and enhancements that support the needs of AU Abroad and the Abroad at AU teams. Maintain, update, and optimize AU Abroad websites and Terra Dotta content—including FAQs, application guidance, and instructional resources—to ensure accuracy, usability, accessibility, and alignment with recruitment goals. Support campus partners whose staff use Terra Dotta by providing guidance, troubleshooting assistance, and documentation. Coordinate with OIT and the vendor to support data synchronization between Terra Dotta and university record systems, including student account setup and maintenance. Continuously assess and improve system use, applying Terra Dotta to new functions and projects; provide training and support to staff to promote consistent and effective use. 3.) Program Operations Support daily operations for designated study abroad cycles or program areas, including updating application materials and pre‑ and post‑decision content in Terra Dotta. Manage process‑based system tasks such as application material audits, form tracking, standard report generation, and data quality checks. Assist with visa‑related administrative tasks, including preparing visa letters, coordinating batch submissions, and assembling standard materials in accordance with established guidelines. Support academic processes related to global programs, including course registration preparation, add/drop tracking, transcript intake, and document verification. Maintain internal tracking tools, shared documentation, and workflows to ensure timely, accurate information exchange across the office. 4.) Student Support and Engagement Provide front‑line support to students exploring global opportunities by responding to inquiries related to program options, eligibility, timelines, and processes. Offer general advising via email, drop‑ins, information sessions, and class visits; triage complex cases to Program Managers or Associate Directors as appropriate. Represent AU Abroad at recruitment and retention events, including admissions, orientation, and campus engagement activities. Proactively communicate with students to support application completion, pre‑departure readiness, and persistence in global programs. Draft, schedule, and distribute high‑impact communications—such as promotional emails, reminder campaigns, event announcements, and onboarding materials—to encourage participation and timely engagement. 5.) Special Projects and Administrative Support Provide administrative and operational support for AU Abroad initiatives, including front‑desk coverage during peak periods or staffing gaps. Support student advising functions as needed. Contribute to departmental and university‑wide projects that advance global engagement, student success, and strategic priorities. Competencies: Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Prioritizing and Organizing. Serving Customers. Supporting Coworkers. Displaying Creativity. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. May occasionally require work on evenings and weekends.  Hybrid working will be offered. Current expectation is 3 days a week on campus, with 2 days per week working remotely. This may change depending on business needs.   This position is union eligible.  Salary Range: $30.22 - $32.97 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience. Preferred Education and Experience: 2 - 4 years of relevant experience. Previous experience with Terra Dotta and website maintenance are strongly preferred. Previous experience with Excel Pivot charts or BI tools preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Excellent planning, project management and facilitation skills with high-level attention to detail.  Ability to multi-task, organize and prioritize while maintaining high standards of accuracy and quality.  Demonstrated organizational skills to establish goals; manage assignments and competing priorities; work under pressure of deadlines; and to follow through to successful completion.   Excellent interpersonal, verbal and written skills, including the ability to develop and sustain relationships with a variety of stakeholders.  Must have the ability to function in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. Ability to work independently. Solid communication and computer skills, along with excellent interpersonal and presentation skills. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/IRW-Social-Video-Designer-Reporter---Researcher--Student-_R5125": {
      "title": "IRW Social Video Designer/Reporter & Researcher (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: School of Communication Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The IRW Social Video Designer handles vertical video and other social design and development for our investigative stories, as well as social media, web production and marketing efforts. Applicants should be undergraduate majors or minors in journalism or related fields. Candidates should be familiar with and have a passion for both investigative reporting and social media design for journalism, including data visualization. IRW is a learning environment, so applicants of varying skill levels are welcome. Students may also work as a researcher and reporter with publishing partners on a variety of subjects. Subjects include, but are not limited to, immigration, public health, and law enforcement. IRW Student Reporters/Researchers report directly to the Executive Editor of the IRW, and will interact with other staff, students, faculty, and consultants of the IRW. This position is open to undergraduate students at American University. This position does not have a Federal Work Study (FWS) Award. Essential Functions: Design and video production. Social design and development. Social media, web production, and marketing. Other duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 hours per week. Salary Range: $22.50 per hour. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Applicants are encouraged to submit a resume and cover letter addressed to IRW’s Executive Editor, Joe Stephens. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/HRL-Office-Assistant--Student-_R5130": {
      "title": "HRL Office Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Housing Assignments Support Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Office Assistant (OA) is a student staff position in Housing & Residence Life (HRL) within American University’s Division of Student Affairs. Reporting to the Housing Assignments team, the OA delivers responsive, professional customer service and administrative support that sustain daily office operations. The OA contributes to a welcoming, well-informed experience for students, families, and campus partners and collaborates with professional and student staff across HRL.  Essential Functions: Serve as the primary point of contact for students, families, and visitors to the HRL office. Assist via phone, email, live chat, and in-person interactions, providing accurate information about housing policies, procedures, and campus resources. Process forms and complete administrative tasks with attention to detail and adherence to established deadlines. Maintain the confidentiality of student records and sensitive information in accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and departmental standards. Support special projects, including document managing and the review of HRL communications and website content for accuracy and consistency. Provide logistical support for departmental events, meetings, and training sessions. Perform other related duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 - 20 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Current enrollment as a undergraduate or graduate student at American University. Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.25, maintained for the duration of employment. Demonstrate organizational, written and verbal communication, problem-solving, and customer service skills. A high standard of professionalism, dependability, and discretion in handling confidential information. Preferred Education and Experience: Previous experience in customer service, reception, or an office environment. Proficiency with Microsoft. Familiarity with American University's residential communities. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Shifts are scheduled during office hours: 9 AM to 5 PM, Monday through Friday. Potential for non-traditional hours. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/WCL-Receptionist--Student---FWS-_R5129": {
      "title": "WCL Receptionist (Student) (FWS)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The student receptionist will provide front‑desk and administrative support for the WCL Clinical Program. Key responsibilities include greeting visitors, answering phones, assisting students and clients with basic inquiries, managing messages, and supporting day‑to‑day office tasks such as filing, scanning, and scheduling. The position may also include occasional language interpretation support. Reports to Lucy Newton, Associate Director, Clinical Program Essential Functions: Greeting visitors. Answering phones. Assisting students and clients with basic inquiries. Managing messages. Supporting day‑to‑day office tasks such as filing, scanning, and scheduling. Other duties as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 10 hours per week. Salary Range: $18.40 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Strong communication and customer‑service skills. Professionalism and reliability. Ability to multitask in a busy office environment. Attention to detail and strong organizational abilities. Basic proficiency with email, calendars, and office software. Language proficiency for interpretation. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Resident-Assistant--Spring--Student-_R5126": {
      "title": "Resident Assistant, Spring (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: Residence Life Training Leadership Programs Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Resident Assistant (RA) is an undergraduate or graduate part-time student staff member of Housing & Residence Life and a member of the University’s Division of Student Affairs. The RA fulfills a vital role in the residence hall community by connecting residents to resources, providing advice on how to navigate the collegiate experience, and creating enriching living environments. The RA reports to the Community Director (CD) and is expected to work closely with other staff members (other RAs, Desk Assistants, Living Learning Communities, Themed Communities, etc.) within the building, as well as across campus. Essential Functions: 1.) Community Engagement Serve as the leader in developing and facilitating an environment on the floor and in the Residence Hall in which students can grow and learn socially as well as academically. Plan and implement learning and engagement opportunities for residents as part of the Eagle Flight Plan, focusing on leadership, self-discovery and community responsibility. Advise and refer their residents to campus resources to aid in supporting their academic, personal, and social well-being. Complete Clawed Chats for their floor/community aimed at developing and building a rapport and relationship with the residents that live in these areas. Submit at least two (2) “Of the Month” award nomination per semester through the National Residence Hall Honorary (NRHH). 2.) Emergency Response Serve in a community-wide on-call rotation. RAs can expect to be on call [regularly, including some weekends. The RA on call must remain in their residential community and be available to respond to emergency concerns. RA on call shifts occur every night from 8 pm - 8 am , and on weekends from 8 am - 8 pm. RA on-call responsibilities include staying in the residence hall to be accessible to residents, responding to any issues that arise, and monitoring the residential environment by (1) Completing community rounds to maintain the safety and security of the building. (2) Ensuring external doors and windows are locked and secured. (3) Reporting communal facilities concerns. (4) Documenting potential policy violations. (5) Acting in the capacity of a Desk Assistant should a coverage issue arise (paid hourly) during on call hours. (6) Providing support and resources to students in need. (7) Granting students access to their rooms if locked out (“lockouts”). RAs are required to serve on call during university breaks and holidays, including Spring Break. RAs may also be directed to serve on call during unexpected university closures. When serving on call, RAs are not permitted at any point to leave their assigned residential community. RAs serving on call are not permitted to take the RA on call phone off campus. RAs are expected to return the on-call phone to its designated location when no longer serving on duty. In the event of a significant residence hall or campus emergency, RAs are expected to assist, if needed.   3.) Administrative Duties Support department-wide initiatives. RA recruitment and selection information sessions, tabling, and interviews.   Other university and departmental events that may require staff assistance. Conduct regular administrative tasks on behalf of Housing & Residence Life, including the completing of Room Inventory Forms (RIFs), documenting potential policy violations, and reporting facilities concerns. Complete Health and Safety Inspections for their floor/community at least two (2) times a year. Complete accurate and detailed incident reports, Equity/Title IX(ETIX) reports and other important reports immediately using either the ETIX link or Guardian software.   4.) Opening & Closing of Residence Halls Help prepare for check-ins, checkouts, openings, and closings. RAs are expected to assist with these duties prior to and at the conclusion of the spring semester.   5.) Desk Assistant Resident Assistants are required to serve 3 hours each week as a Desk Assistant in their assigned community, which is included in their compensation package. RAs are permitted to work additional hours at the front desk at the Desk Assistant hourly wage rate. Resident Assistants are required to participate in scheduled online or in-person training prior to the start of the spring semesters. Resident Assistants are also expected to participate in ongoing development through in-service meetings. RAs are expected and required to be at all components of fall and spring training. No Resident Assistant is excused. Resident Assistants are required to attend weekly staff meetings. RAs are not permitted to schedule classes or other commitments during this time. RAs are also expected to participate in regular one-on-one supervisory meetings.   6.) Outside Involvement and Employment After academic commitments, the RA position will be the staff member’s priority. Housing & Residence Life, in consultation with the RA involved, reserves the right to limit time commitments that may interfere with their job performance. Outside commitments include other student leadership/organization positions, additional jobs, non-academic credit internships, etc. Resident Assistants are permitted to maintain outside commitments with prior approval from your direct supervisor. Academic student internships are limited to three (3) credits per semester. Resident Assistants must submit a written request about any additional job, internship or University leadership responsibilities detailing the anticipated time commitment to their direct supervisor within 48 business hours of receiving the offer. Prior approval is required for participating in other University Leadership positions (e.g., Orientation Coordinators/Leaders, Student Government , etc.). Due to conflicting responsibilities, RAs are not permitted to be hired as Desk Coordinators, or to be elected or appointed members of the Residence Hall Association.   Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 15 hours per week. Salary Range: $375 stipend per month. Required Education and Experience: Full-time enrollment as an undergraduate or graduate student (minimum 12 credits and a maximum of 17 per semester for undergrad & minimum 9 credits and a maximum of 12 per semester for graduate students). If a Resident Assistant wishes to drop below the minimum credit hours, they must receive written permission from the Director of Residence Life in order to retain the RA position. Complete one (1) semester of full-time undergraduate education by the start of employment. One (1) semester living on campus at American University. Cumulative GPA at or above 2.5, and term GPA at or above 2.5 (GPAs must be maintained from the date of application until the date of separation) Must not have been found responsible for violating a serious conduct policy, residence hall regulations, or University Policy (must be maintained from the date of application to the date of separation). All applicants must attend an information session by December.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: This is a 5-month live-in position from January through May. The RA responsibilities and time commitment are determined by the needs of the department. The RA role requires flexibility to support an occasionally unpredictable environment. Housing credit added to the student account to cover the cost of a single room in the assigned residence hall. Resident Assistants are not required to have a meal plan. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/Legal-Education-Advisor_R5104": {
      "title": "Legal Education Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The primary function of this position is to promote the academic excellence of American University Washington College of Law students, from matriculation through graduation. The Legal Education Advisor (LEA) provides all law students individualized advising on their academic progress and identifies and develops resources for academic and bar exam success. The LEA also will serve as the assigned advisor to students with Academic Alert status, which includes mandatory meetings and workshops. The LEA will provide strategic counseling and best practices for students to develop their academic skills and achievement both in law school and on the bar exam. The LEA will maintain an awareness of best practices for learning strategies, bar exam preparation, and provide students with feedback, resources, and advice about academic skills including the process of legal analysis, exam writing, and time management. Essential Functions: 1.) Academic Development Advise all law students on best practices for developing the necessary skills for academic and professional success. Evaluate student needs and provide resources for academic success. Develop individualized academic recovery plans for students on Academic Alert status. Create study plans and provide exam strategies to improve academic performance for all students. Conduct workshops to develop law students’ study skills, time management, critical thinking, and analytical skills. 2.) Bar Advising Advise all law students on best practices for bar exam planning and success. Ensure law students are aware of bar exam requirements and other bar exam matters. Facilitate group and individual advising on bar exam preparation including, but not limited to, bar exam subject matter, format, scoring, bar exam testing strategies, selecting a bar exam jurisdiction, bar exam financial considerations, and bar preparation plans. Monitor and evaluate student progress during the bar preparation period. Advise students on best practices for completing bar preparation courses. 3.) Programming/Instruction Develop and facilitate workshops and other educational programs designed to assist academic and bar exam success. Identify content and opportunities to collaborate with faculty, student groups, offices, and programs to address academic achievement and bar exam readiness. 4.) Professional Development Participate in professional organizations related to law school academic and bar exam success. Keep abreast of best practices and resources for student learning and bar exam readiness. 5.) Other Tasks Assist the Assistant Dean and other team members with advising, programming, outreach, and engagement as directed. Work closely with team members to ensure consistent messaging under the guidance of the Assistant Dean. Complete projects and assignments as tasked to assist with the overall goals of the office. Supervisory Responsibility: May supervise student and/or administrative personnel. Competencies: Championing Customer Needs. Building and Supporting Teams. Developing Plans. Evaluating and Implementing Ideas. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Some evening and weekend hours required. This is a union-eligible position. Salary Range: $76,000.00 - $80,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Juris Doctor or equivalent. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience. Preferred Education and Experience: Juris Doctor. 3 - 5 years of relevant experience. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Must possess excellent interpersonal, organizational, and oral and written communication skills. Proficiency at project management, including, but not limited to, developing, planning, and implementing goals. Ability to maintain accurate records for consistent feedback. Ability to collect, interpret, and analyze data. Ability to work collaboratively with all members of the WCL community. Prior academic or bar support teaching experience – or suitable combination of two to four years of practice experience and adjunct teaching. Prior experience advising or mentoring law students and/or law graduates, preferably in the area of bar preparation or academic support. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Assistant-Director-Financial-Aid_R4647": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Financial Aid",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Financial Aid Communication & Service Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: This position plays a key role in the administration and oversight of American University's financial aid programs, with primary responsibility for the daily service delivery operations within the Office of Financial Aid and the administration of Yellow Ribbon Program. The position manages day-to-day service delivery operations by supervising customer service representative staff, ensuring adequate front desk coverage, monitoring phone agent availability and service levels, compiling and disseminating monthly service metrics, and assisting with troubleshooting disruptions related to Webex phone, ServiceNow CRM, and Zoom Scheduler. The Assistant Director manages Yellow Ribbon Program coordination with the Office of Admissions, Veteran Services Office, Student Accounts, Washington College of Law, and Office of Graduate Studies; oversees timely identification, awarding, revision, and reconciliation of Yellow Ribbon awards; and coordinates the annual calculation, update, and submission of the university's Yellow Ribbon Program application. The incumbent also advises students and families, supports staff training and case management, and ensures effective, student-centered service delivery. Essential Functions: 1.) Financial Aid Office Service Delivery Management Manage the day-to-day service delivery operations of the Office of Financial Aid. Supervise customer service representative staff; ensure adequate coverage at the financial aid front desk; monitor phone agent availability and service levels; compile and disseminate monthly service metrics, including phone and walk-in statistics; and assist in troubleshooting disruptions related to Webex phone, ServiceNow CRM, and Zoom Scheduler. Support consistent, responsive, and student-centered service delivery across communication channels 2.) Management of the Yellow Ribbon Program Manage the Yellow Ribbon Program in coordination with the Office of Admissions, Veteran Services Office, Student Accounts, Washington College of Law, and Office of Graduate Studies. Identify eligible students in a timely manner; award, revise, and reconcile Yellow Ribbon awards; and coordinate with university stakeholders to annually calculate, update, and submit the Yellow Ribbon Program application. Ensure program administration aligns with applicable federal, institutional, and university requirements. 3.) Counseling and Financial Aid Advising Advise and counsel prospective and enrolled students, families, and university administrators regarding federal, state, and institutional aid programs. Explain regulations, policies, compliance expectations, need analysis, verification requirements, budgeting considerations, and the application of aid within the financial aid process. 4.) Training, Case Management, and Reconciliation Train financial aid staff and support case management by maintaining deep knowledge of federal and institutional regulations and office procedures. Reconcile student records and aid activity as needed, support issue resolution, and promote consistent application of policies, procedures, and service standards across the office. Supervisory Responsibility: Yes. Supervises customer service representative staff and one Financial Aid Counselor. Competencies: Serving Customers. Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Making Accurate Judgments and Decisions. Championing Customer Needs. Building and Supporting Teams. Managing Talent. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Salary Range: $70,000.00 - $80,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 3 - 5 years of relevant experience. Financial aid administration and counseling experience required. Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree or equivalent. Experience with automated systems and strong written and verbal communication skills preferred. Travel Required: Minimal travel may be required for conferences and professional development activities. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Spring-Valley-Campus-Washington-DC/Center-for-Latin-American---Latino-Studies-Assistant--Student-_R3956": {
      "title": "Center for Latin American & Latino Studies Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nWork Where You Learn: Build Experience, Grow Skills, and Contribute to Your University Community.   This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Most student positions at American University are eligible to use Federal Work Study (FWS) awards, with a few exceptions. FWS funds cannot be applied to janitorial, construction, partisan or sectarian positions. For information or questions regarding FWS funds, please contact American University's Office of Financial Aid.   Important guidance for current American University employees: American University current employees, including those employed in student positions, must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into your employee Workday account and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Applying outside of your employee Workday account may cause delays in a hire process. Department: CLALS Operations Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Summary: The Center for Latin American & Latino Studies (CLALS) engages scholars and practitioners to promote cutting-edge research to enrich understanding of Latin America and of Latino communities in the US. CLALS is  hiring   student s. Student Assistants will be expected to provide research, administrative, and logistical support for the Center for Latin America & Latino Studies’ Director, faculty, staff, and fellows, as called upon. Responsibilities will likely include assisting with the collection and processing of project data and event preparation. Essential Functions: Provide research, administrative, and logistical support for the Center for Latin America & Latino Studies’ Director, faculty, staff, and fellows, as called upon . Assist with the collection and processing of project data and event preparation.  Other duties assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 1 5 - 25 hours per week. Salary Range: $20.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Candidates must be  student s in good standing in one of American University’s programs. Applicants must be dependable, show attention to detail, have the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously, set priorities, and meet deadlines. Excellent research, writing, and editing ability are essential along with good computer and IT skills.  Preferred Education and Experience: Preference will be given to candidates who are studying fields related to Latin America and/or Latino communities in the US and have strong Spanish/and or Portuguese language skills. Production skills such as creating videos, podcasts, digital editing, and infographics are highly desirable. Other Details This position is available only to enrolled American University students. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Visit https://www.american.edu/hr/ for additional information about American University employment and benefits.   Current American University Employees American University current employees (including those employed in student positions) must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings.   Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu .   American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Adjunct--Film-and-Media-Arts-Division--School-of-Communication--Open-Continuous-_R1026-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Film and Media Arts Division, School of Communication (Open Continuous)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: School of Communication Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Exempt Job Description: This is an open continuous vacancy announcement that will be used to fill adjunct vacancies as they occur. Until you hear from a representative of the School of Communication or the Office of HR Faculty, please continue to also apply directly to other positions posted on AU's website. Summary: We’re excited that you are applying to become a member of the Adjunct Faculty in the Film and Media Arts Division at American University. Adjunct faculty are a key component of the university community, enriching the curriculum with their professional experience and scholarly expertise. They play a vital role in every department and program in every school and college at the university, teaching on campus, in our on-line programs, and working with students one-on-one. The American University School of Communication empowers undergraduates and graduates in its programs to tell stories that influence change, inspire action, and transform our communities and our world.  Most of our bachelor of arts programs will hone your professional skills for audio, video, mobile, and online platforms. You'll build a core knowledge and bolster that with solid fundamentals in communication and media theory and research, writing, editing, and media production.  Our graduate programs will build your competence and knowledge as a multi-platform communicator. We will teach you the in-demand skills critical to your professional success. You will also learn the critical theory and fundamental underpinnings to sustain your career well into the future.  With Washington, D.C., one of the most exciting, influential, and dynamic cities in the world, as your classroom, you'll have opportunities and internships that will open the door to a career in the communication industry. The Film & Media Arts Division offers a broad, theory- and skills-based media education including fiction and non-fiction production, screenwriting, photography, immersive filmmaking, and game design. There is considerable flexibility in our students’ course of study, allowing them to find the specific area of filmmaking that appeals to them most. FMA recognizes that student interests may evolve over the course of our program and we are committed to guiding them as they find their calling. We are committed to diversity and inclusivity, and to giving voice and vision to those who are often underrepresented in our professions.   Since the publication of the first Code of Best Practices for Sustainable Filmmaking in 2009 by the Center for Environmental Filmmaking and the Center for Media and Social Impact, the division has focused attention on sustainability in filmmaking from fiction to documentary. FMA is a member of the UFVA’s Green Film School Alliance and is committed to saving the planet one film at a time. Make your mark, author your story, and shape your future. Find your place at the American University School of Communication.  3-credit course rate range: $5,163-$5,900 Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Hiring offers for this position are contingent on the successful completion of a background check. Please begin the appointment/reappointment approval process by applying below. American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities. To ensure the health and safety of our community AU requires COVID-19 vaccinations for faculty and staff. Click here to learn more about our health and safety directive. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/Circulation-Manager_R5092": {
      "title": "Circulation Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Full On Campus Presence Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Circulation Manager coordinates day-to-day access services operations at the Pence Law Library and provides senior on-site coverage during assigned shifts, including evenings and weekends. Working with the Access Services Librarian and the other Circulation Manager or Managers, as applicable, the position supports the delivery and continuous improvement of circulation, course reserves, interlibrary loan, consortium lending, patron account services, collection access, study-space and equipment services, marketing, outreach, and related patron services. The Circulation Manager supervises assigned part-time staff and provides day-to-day direction, training, and support to part-time and student employees. The position uses Ex Libris Alma, interlibrary loan and consortium systems, Microsoft 365, social media platforms, Springshare products, and other library technologies to manage workflows, maintain accurate records, communicate with patrons, promote library resources and services, and support departmental assessment. The position exercises independent judgment in resolving routine service, staffing, facilities, technology, and patron concerns; documents and escalates significant matters; and contributes recommendations concerning policies, procedures, communications, and departmental priorities. Essential Functions: 1.) Access Services Operations and Patron Experience Coordinates daily circulation desk operations and provides direct desk coverage, including opening and closing responsibilities as assigned. Performs and resolves circulation, patron-account, room-use, equipment, course reserve, and collection-access transactions. Provides directional and informational assistance, basic research triage, and referrals to librarians and other law school offices. Serves as the senior library staff member on site during assigned evening and weekend shifts, responds to routine incidents, and contacts appropriate personnel when a matter exceeds delegated authority. Applies library policies consistently, resolves routine exceptions, addresses service concerns, and communicates recurring patron needs or operational problems to the Access Services Librarian.     2.) Staff Supervision, Scheduling, and Training Directly supervises assigned part-time non-student employees and provides day-to-day work direction to student employees. Participates in recruitment, interviewing, onboarding, scheduling, work assignment, timekeeping review, and semester staffing transitions. Develops and delivers training, cross-training, procedures, checklists, and service standards for circulation desk employees. Provides coaching and performance feedback, documents attendance or performance concerns, and supports employee evaluation and performance-management processes as assigned. Coordinates shift coverage and communicates staffing, training, supply, and operational needs to the Access Services Librarian. 3.) Resource Sharing and Course Reserves Processes borrowing and lending requests through interlibrary loan and WRLC consortium systems and ensures that materials move accurately and promptly through each workflow. Pulls, scans, ships, receives, and processes requested materials; monitors requests; resolves routine exceptions; and communicates with patrons and partner institutions. Receives and tracks faculty course reserve requests, creates and updates reserve records, processes materials, and removes outdated reserve items at the end of each term. Coordinates with faculty, liaison librarians, acquisitions, cataloging, and other library units when materials must be located, purchased, described, or made accessible. Follows established copyright, licensing, privacy, and document-delivery procedures and refers unusual requests for librarian review. 4.) Library Systems, Patron Accounts, and Workflow Administration Uses Ex Libris Alma and related platforms to maintain accurate patron, item, loan, request, fulfillment, and course reserve records. Resolves routine patron-account matters involving borrowing status, overdue, lost, damaged, billed, or replacement materials within delegated authority. Troubleshoots routine library-system, printing, scanning, reservation, and service technology problems and refers complex or recurring issues to the appropriate unit. Creates and maintains internal procedures, forms, tutorials, guides, webpages, FAQs, shared files, and other documentation for circulation and resource-sharing services. Supports testing and implementation of new systems, technologies, policies, and workflows and helps train staff on approved changes. 5.) Marketing, Outreach, and Social Media Develops and contributes accurate, accessible, audience-appropriate content for library social media, webpages, digital signage, newsletters, email communications, and printed promotional materials. Maintains a departmental content calendar and coordinates scheduled communications with the Access Services Librarian and other library personnel. Promotes library resources, services, collections, spaces, programs, events, course reserves, interlibrary loan, study aids, and other student-support initiatives. Participates in orientations, tours, tabling, welcome programs, student organization events, and outreach to faculty, journals, clinics, programs, and law school offices. Tracks basic engagement and participation information, gathers user feedback, and recommends adjustments to outreach and communication strategies.           6.) Collections, Spaces, Equipment, and Facilities Monitors study rooms, reservation compliance, public service areas, library equipment, displays, signage, and furniture to support a safe, accessible, and effective learning environment. Responds to and documents routine facilities, technology, accessibility, safety, security, and building-access concerns and promptly reports matters requiring additional assistance. Performs and coordinates shelving, shelf-reading, inventory, shifting, collection relocation, and related stacks-maintenance projects. Identifies and helps resolve problems involving item records, labels, signage, physical condition, availability, lost or damaged materials, and collection organization. Maintains departmental supplies and service equipment and collaborates with Access Services, Technical Services, facilities, and technology personnel on related workflows. 7.) Assessment, Planning, Projects, and Professional Responsibilities Compiles and verifies circulation, interlibrary loan, course reserve, room-use, seat-count, staffing, outreach, and social media statistics. Identifies patterns, recurring problems, and opportunities for improvement and prepares reports or recommendations for the Access Services Librarian. Participates in policy and procedure development, departmental planning, service assessment, workflow review, and implementation projects. Participates in library and university meetings, training, and professional-development activities and maintains awareness of developments in access services, resource sharing, library technology, and user engagement. Performs other related duties and special projects as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: Each Circulation Manager indirectly helps supervise part-time staff. Helps assist with supervising day to day work of part time staff and provides day-to-day direction, scheduling, training, coaching, and performance feedback to student employees. The position participates in hiring, onboarding, timekeeping review, evaluation, and documentation of employee performance as assigned. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week, with full on-campus presence. Regular evening and weekend hours are required. The established schedule may vary during examination periods, summer sessions, university breaks, holidays, staffing shortages, and emergencies. Depending on the shift, the Circulation Manager may serve as the sole law library or law school staff member on site. The position must be able to work independently, exercise sound judgment, follow emergency and incident-response procedures, and communicate significant matters promptly. This position enables the library to maintain a full-time staff presence during extended operating hours. The position is considered essential and may be required to provide coverage for open shifts or emergencies in accordance with university policy. Salary Range: $23.21 - $27.00 per hour.             Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education, training, and relevant experience. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience Experience in library services, higher education, customer service operations, or comparable environment. Experience training employees, coordinating workflows, or leading shifts is required. Preferred Education and Experience: Juris Doctor. Master of Library and Information Science (MLIS); or a comparable graduate degree. For library and information science degrees, graduation from an American Library Association-accredited program is preferred. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience Experience in an academic, research, or law library. At least one year of formal supervisory or staff-management experience. Experience using Ex Libris Alma, particularly fulfillment, circulation, patron services, requests, or course reserves. Experience with interlibrary loan, document delivery, consortium resource sharing, or course reserves. Experience developing marketing, outreach, social media, digital signage, or public engagement content. Experience with Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Springshare products, Canva or comparable design tools, web content management systems, or online reservation systems. Familiarity with legal education, legal research, or law library services. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Advanced proficiency with word processing, spreadsheets, email, shared-document platforms, online databases, and other office productivity applications. Ability to learn and effectively use integrated library systems, interlibrary loan systems, room-reservation platforms, social media tools, content-management systems, and other library technologies. Strong written, oral, interpersonal, organizational, customer-service, and problem-solving skills. Ability to create clear, accurate, accessible, and audience-appropriate instructions, promotional materials, and digital communications. Ability to manage competing priorities, maintain accurate records, protect patron privacy, and handle challenging individuals or situations with tact, professionalism, and poise. Ability to work independently as senior staff on site and to make timely decisions within established policies and delegated authority. Ability to lift and move library materials, equipment, and packages weighing up to 50 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Director-of-Strategic-Communications_R5100": {
      "title": "Director of Strategic Communications",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Kogod School of Business Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: Leads the School’s communications efforts, which include developing communication plans; design and production of integrated communication campaigns; administration of communication budgets; management of external vendor relationships; and collaboration with university offices including University Communications and Marketing. The position guides the brand and reputation of the school with an eye on positioning, message impact, alignment with other university communications, and adherence to brand standards. The position works collaboratively with internal and external partners, vendors and agencies and directs the communications of KSB including presentations and reports on behalf of the Dean. The position will hold primary responsibility for Kogod website content. This position is responsible for managing direct reports as well as student workers.   Essential Functions: 1.) Communication Branding: Establish, advance, and execute messaging and identity for the Kogod School of Business, in coordination with university identity standards. Develops the School’s visual identity and designs and produces integrated marketing collateral materials that promote academic programs, services, and faculty. Content: Direct a refined content strategy for business school. Ensure competitive positioning, search optimization, efficient use of resources, and communication workflow among program offices, faculty departments, and other key stakeholders. Works closely with the assistant dean and senior staff to identify communication priorities. Collaborates in the production of all publications; including video, print publications (collateral materials), email newsletters, and others. Web: Includes oversight for kogod.american.edu, social media channels, email campaigns/communications, multimedia, externally hosted websites, and apps. Monitoring of Kogod’s reputation online, including inclusion or exclusion from other digital portals and forums. Communication: Manage KSB communications to internal and external constituencies including reports, presentations and messages by the Dean. Review and vet KSB messaging for signature/special events (Orientation, Commencement, Lecture Series) in conjunction with KSB Senior Leadership and Events team.   2.)  Media Relations Work with AU Communications, PR partner, and media outlets to coordinate opportunities for KSB faculty and staff in the media and in any public space.  Develop media relations strategy for KSB faculty and staff.  Provide media training in conjunction with the University Communications. Assist Kogod faculty in creating a strategy to communicate the public impact of their scholarship.   3.) Administration/Management Direct workflow of communications staff. Manage contracts, including bidding, negotiating, invoicing, and vendor evaluation. Issue Requests for Proposals (RFPs) and evaluate responses. Liaison across campus and within School, working with University’s marketing, media relations, publications and information technology offices to coordinate resources and ensure compliance with campus wide efforts. Involved and counsel on school activities related to image, visuals, and rankings.     4.) Other Duties as Assigned Supervisory Responsibility: Supervises the following position(s): Senior Designer, Communications Manager, Social Media Coordinator, Senior Digital Designer, and Senior Videographer. Competencies: Acting Strategically. Evaluating and Implementing Ideas. Displaying Creativity. Developing Plans. Leading and Inspiring People. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Salary Range: $103,000.00 - $115,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree. 8 - 10 years of relevant experience.   Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree.   Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Deep understanding of online marketing and communications, specifically writing for the web, social media and project management experience. Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills. Ability to communicate and build long term relationships with on campus and off campus partners, vendors and agencies and coordinate with on campus resources. Ability to multi-task and meet deadlines while paying close attention to detail. Proficient computer skills including the Microsoft office suite, Adobe Suite, web graphics, video editing, database development, and the tools required to fulfill the position’s responsibilities as technology evolves. Ability to manage and prioritize multiple tasks with particular attention to detail. Knowledge of guerrilla marketing tactics and social media strategies. Experience managing direct reports. Expertise in strategic planning, professional marketing and brand leadership, and audience insight. A strategic thinker with a natural curiosity to continually improve results and experiment with new methods and ideas. Demonstrated ability to use and interpret data to inform marketing decisions. Familiarity with marketing tools, such as HubSpot or Salesforce. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Manager--Marketing-Operations_R5101": {
      "title": "Manager, Marketing Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Kogod School of Business Time Type: Full time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Exempt Work Modality: Hybrid 01 (On Campus 3-4 Days/Week) Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: This position leads digital marketing for the Kogod School of Business, with end-to-end ownership of the School's marketing technology ecosystem, constituent communication journeys, website, and performance analytics. The role plans and executes the School's digital marketing strategy in support of enrollment, brand awareness, and engagement goals across prospective students, current students, alumni, and partners. The position serves as the School's lead HubSpot administrator, and is accountable for marketing automation, email marketing, audience segmentation, landing pages, and data-driven journey design. It owns campaign measurement and attribution — establishing KPIs, producing regular performance and budget reporting, and translating results into recommendations for the marketing team, Admissions, and program leadership. This position supervises one Marketing Automation Specialist and student workers, and works collaboratively with the marketing team, Admissions, program offices, and UCM. This role reports to the interim Assistant Dean of Marketing & Strategy Essential Functions: 1.) Digital Marketing Strategy and Campaign Planning Plans and manages the annual digital marketing calendar for the School and its programs in collaboration with the Assistant Dean, Admissions, and program leadership. Develops integrated inbound campaigns spanning email, landing pages, web, paid and organic digital channels, and social. Coordinates campaign assets and timelines with the content and design team. Identifies audience and funnel-stage priorities and recommends channel mix and tactics to meet enrollment and engagement goals. 2.) Marketing Automation and Constituent Journeys Owns the design and delivery of school-wide communication journeys in HubSpot for prospects, applicants, admitted and current students, alumni, and other constituents. Directs audience segmentation, workflow architecture, personalization, and lead scoring. Ensures campaigns are built, tested, monitored, and optimized against goals, including A/B and multivariate testing. Sets email best-practice and compliance standards for the School and reviews campaigns produced by the Marketing Automation Specialist and partner offices. 3.) Analytics, Reporting, and Attribution Establishes and monitors KPIs across website, email, landing pages, blog, social, and paid media. Conducts enrollment funnel and attribution analysis and produces regular campaign performance and health reports for the marketing team, Admissions, School leadership, and program leadership. Builds and maintains HubSpot and Google Analytics dashboards. Performs competitive and market research and uses findings to recommend new tactics and improve results. 4.) Website and Digital Content Holds primary responsibility for conversion pages on kogod.american.edu in the HubSpot CMS, including program pages, landing pages, blog, and SEO. Manages the web request and maintenance workflow, maintains design-system and brand-standards consistency, and leads efforts to improve user experience across devices using traffic and behavior data. Advises staff and faculty on web accessibility compliance and represents the School in university-wide web forums. 5.) Marketing Technology Administration and Integration Serves as administrator of the School's marketing technology stack, including HubSpot (Marketing, CMS, and CRM), SMS and related platforms, and project management tools. Owns the HubSpot–Salesforce integration in partnership with Admissions and university IT, including data hygiene, field mapping, sync monitoring, and issue resolution. Evaluates and implements new platform features and integrations, maintains documentation, and trains team members and partner offices on the tools. 6.) Supervision and Team Leadership Supervises one Marketing Automation Specialist and student workers, including hiring, onboarding, work assignment, coaching, and performance management. Sets priorities and quality standards for the digital marketing function and builds the team's capability in automation, analytics, and emerging tools, including AI-assisted marketing practices. 7.) Other Duties as Assigned Supervisory Responsibility: The Marketing Automation Specialist will report to this role and the role will also supervise the departments student workers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full-time. 35 hours per week. Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $85,000.00 annually. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent in marketing, communications, business, or a related field. 5 - 8 years of relevant experience. Progressively responsible experience in digital marketing, demand generation, or marketing automation. Demonstrated hands-on expertise in HubSpot or a comparable marketing automation and CRM platform, including workflow configuration, segmentation, email marketing, and reporting. Experience managing a website in a content management system and applying SEO and accessibility best practices. Experience establishing KPIs, building dashboards, and analyzing campaign and funnel performance using Google Analytics and similar tools. Experience leading or coordinating the work of others, and managing vendors and budgets. Strong written and verbal communication skills; ability to present data and recommendations to leadership. Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree in marketing, business, analytics, or a related field. 8 - 10 years of relevant experience. Experience in higher education or enrollment marketing. Experience administering a HubSpot–Salesforce (or similar CRM) integration. HubSpot certifications (Inbound Marketing, Marketing Software, CMS) and/or Google Analytics certification. Experience managing direct reports. Working knowledge of HTML and CSS; experience with SMS marketing platforms and paid digital media. Familiarity with AI tools applied to marketing workflows, content, and analysis. Travel Required: Minimal; occasional local travel for events, conferences, or vendor meetings. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Deep, hands-on command of HubSpot (Marketing Hub, CMS Hub, CRM) and CRM integrations, with the judgment to architect systems rather than simply operate them. Data fluency: ability to define KPIs, build dashboards, analyze funnel and attribution data, and translate findings into clear recommendations for non-technical audiences. Strong web and content acumen, including SEO, UX, accessibility, and CMS management; writes and edits clearly for the web. Curiosity and a test-and-learn mindset; willingness to adopt new tools, including AI-enabled marketing capabilities, to improve results. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite, Google Analytics, and the tools required to fulfill the position's responsibilities as technology evolves. Ability to manage and prioritize multiple projects with close attention to detail and deadlines. Knowledge of email marketing compliance requirements (e.g., CAN-SPAM) and web accessibility standards (WCAG). Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Part-Time-Athletics-Media---Communications-Support-Staff_R5098": {
      "title": "Part-Time Athletics Media & Communications Support Staff",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Athletics Digital Media Communications Time Type: Part time Job Type: Casual FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: Assist in all aspects of Gameday run-of-show, promotions, script preparation and review and creating a great gameday experience for all constituents.  Essential Functions:  1.) Event Planning and In-Game Execution Collaborate with marketing and sponsorship teams to outline scripts, organize promotional gear, and set up interactive concourse zones. Coordinate and run live fan contests, media timeout promotions, and special presentations for volleyball, basketball, and wrestling.    2.) Fan Interaction & Sponsor Fulfillment Engage directly with students, donors, and fans to drive energy, distribute premiums, and maximize crowd participation. Assist with corporate partner activations and sponsor-driven contests are executed seamlessly and professionally. 3.) Spirit & Culture Building Work as a dynamic member of a fast-acting crew dedicated to building long-term fan loyalty and campus spirit. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 15 hours per week.  Gameday work from August through March. Salary Range: $25.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 1 year of relevant experience. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Tenley-Campus-Washington-DC/Part-Time-Circulation-Assistant_R5093": {
      "title": "Part-Time Circulation Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: Washington College of Law Time Type: Part time Job Type: Regular FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Union: SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division This position is part of a collective bargaining unit represented by SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. That means the terms and conditions of your employment are governed by university policy (including the Staff Personnel Policies Manual) and any collective bargaining agreement entered into between American University and SEIU Local 500 - Provost & Enrollment Division. Job Description: Summary: The Circulation Assistant works on a team consisting of other Circulation Assistants, many of whom are current students, Circulation Managers, and the Assistant Law Librarian to provide outstanding customer service at the Circulation Desk of a busy Law Library that primarily serves students, faculty, and staff of the Washington College of Law, but also serves alumni, members of the bar, and the public. The Circulation Assistant will also be tasked with assignments away from the desk to support access to the library’s resources, study spaces, and services. Essential Functions: 1.) Access Services Operations and Patron Experience Provides direct desk coverage, including opening and closing responsibilities as assigned, during the week and weekends in the morning, afternoon, or evening. Performs and resolves circulation, patron-account, room-use, equipment, course reserve, and collection-access transactions. Provides directional and informational assistance, basic research triage, and referrals to librarians and other law school offices. Responds to routine incidents, and contacts appropriate personnel when a matter exceeds delegated authority. Applies library policies consistently, resolves routine exceptions, addresses service concerns, and communicates recurring patron needs or operational problems to a Circulation Manager or the Access Services Librarian. 2.) Collections, Spaces, Equipment, and Facilities Following stated procedures and checklists, monitors study rooms, reservation compliance, public service areas, library equipment, displays, signage, and furniture to support a safe, accessible, and effective learning environment. Per provided instructions, checks and documents routine facilities, technology, accessibility, safety, security, and building-access concerns and promptly reports matters requiring additional assistance. Per provided instructions, performs and shelf-reading, inventory, shifting, collection relocation, and related stacks-maintenance projects. Per provided instructions, performs patron counts. Identifies, helps resolve, and reports problems involving item records, labels, signage, physical condition, availability, lost or damaged materials, and collection organization. Assists in maintaining departmental supplies and service equipment. 3.) Marketing, Outreach, and Social Media Observes patron behavior and makes suggestions to assist the Circulation Managers to develop accurate, accessible, audience-appropriate content for library social media, webpages, digital signage, newsletters, email communications, and printed promotional materials. Assists with promoting library resources, services, collections, spaces, programs, events, course reserves, interlibrary loan, study aids, and other student-support initiatives. Participates in orientations, tours, tabling, welcome programs, student organization events, and other outreach, as assigned. 4.) Other Related Duties as Assigned Complete other related duties as assigned. Other related duties will be similar in scope and function to other duties and are intended to further the mission of the department. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 27 hours per week. Salary Range: $20.11 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 1 - 3 years of relevant experience. Preferred Education and Experience: Juris Doctor or equivalent. 2 - 4 years of relevant experience. Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Part-Time-Grant-Writer--Researcher--Temporary-_R5094": {
      "title": "Part-Time Grant Writer, Researcher (Temporary)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Work Modality: Union: Excluded Job Description: Summary: American University Museum (AUM) and the Alper Initiative for Washington Art (AIWA) seeks an articulate and strategic Grant Writer / Researcher to work with American University Museum and The College of Arts and Sciences University Advancement (UA) staff to help secure funding from government, corporate, and private foundations to support exhibitions, local artists, and education and community programs, and fuel the overall growth, of the Alper Initiative for Washington Art.   The Alper Initiative for Washington Art is an artist-centered gathering and exhibition space where the creative voices and local artists of the Washington, D.C. region are showcased, amplified, and brought into dialogue with the broader currents of contemporary art.   Essential Functions: 1.) Prospect Research Research, identify, and review federal, state, public and private foundation and corporate funding opportunities and evaluate strategic alignment with AU, AU Museum and the Alper Initiative for Washington Art to determine grants to pursue. Analyze funder giving histories, average award sizes, giving priorities, and geographic and any other relevant restrictions. 2.) Grant and Program Proposals Write narrative proposal for specialized projects including exhibitions, curatorial research, local DMV artist, curator and community outreach.   3.) Grant Lifecycle Tracking Assist in setting AUM’s grant calendar to track letter of inquiry (LOI) dates, proposal deadlines and pre-award logistics. 4.) Funder Stewardship Help build lasting relationships with foundation officers, government representatives and corporate sponsors through strategic communication and updates.                  Competencies: Acquiring and Analyzing Information. Serving Customers. Prioritizing and Organizing. Displaying Creativity. Supporting Coworkers. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Part-time. 3 - 5 hours per week. This is a temporary part-time position ending on or before 6 months. Continuation of the program/position is contingent upon external funding. Salary Range: $28.00 - $32.00 per hour. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree or equivalent. 3 - 5 years of relevant experience.   Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree or equivalent. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: Experience working within a university system.   Other Duties: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
    },
    "https://american.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/AU/job/Main-Campus-Washington-DC/Adjunct-Faculty---CAS-Department-of-Art_R940": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - CAS Department of Art (Open Continuous)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nAmerican University is a student-centered research institution located in Washington, DC, with highly-ranked schools and colleges, internationally-renowned faculty, and a reputation for creating meaningful change in the world. Learn more about American University Department: College of Arts & Sciences Time Type: Part time FLSA Status: Exempt Job Description: This is an open continuous vacancy announcement that will be used to fill adjunct vacancies as they occur. Until you hear from a representative of the Department of Art or the Office of HR Faculty, please continue to also apply directly to other positions posted on AU's website. The Department of Art in the College of Arts and Sciences at American University invites applications for a number of adjunct faculty positions for upcoming Academic Years. We seek applications for candidates qualified to teach in the fields of Art History (BA and/or MA), Graphic Design (BA), and Studio Art (BA and/or MFA). Rank will depend on an applicant’s highest degree earned in Art. The applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The Department is organized under the College of Arts and Sciences, which is where scholarship in the Arts, Humanities, and Sciences is pursued.  Learn more about the College of Arts and Sciences at https://www.american.edu/cas/ and the Department of Art at https://www.american.edu/cas/art/ . The Department of Art in the College of Arts and Sciences has the following adjunct salary ranges: Candidates Without a Terminal Degree In Course Subject Area 1-2 Credit Course: $2,865 3-4 Credit Course: $4,725 5-6 Credit Course: $4,938 Candidates With a Terminal Degree In Course Subject Area 1-2 Credit Course: $3,414 3-4 Credit Course: $5,400 5-6 Credit Course: $5,548 Benefits AU offers a competitive benefits package.  Click here to learn about American University's unique benefit options . Other Details Hiring offers for this position are contingent on successful completion of a background check. Employees in staff positions at American University must deliver their services to the university from either the District of Columbia, Maryland, or Virginia, or perform work on-site at the university. Please note this job announcement is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. American University is an E-Verify employer. Current American University Employees American University current employees must apply through their employee Workday account. If you are a current employee at American University, please log into Workday and select the Find Jobs report which will take you to our internal career listings. Contact Us For more information or assistance with the American University careers site, email  theworkline@american.edu . American University is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution that operates in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The university does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy), age, sexual orientation, disability, marital status, personal appearance, gender identity and expression, family responsibilities, political affiliation, source of income, veteran status, an individual’s genetic information or any other bases under federal or local laws (collectively \"Protected Bases\") in its programs and activities."
